/* Linux: "Explained step by step" walkthroughs. */

explain('l1',`
<p>Almost every server, Docker container and test robot in the world runs Linux, and none of them has a mouse. You move around them by typing. Learn to find your way with a handful of short words and you can work on any computer on the planet.</p>

${V.card(1,'One big tree','every file has one address',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 212" role="img" aria-label="The Linux folder tree: root at the top, then etc, home and var; home holds you; you holds Documents, projects and notes.txt">
<rect class="bx-dark" x="180" y="8" width="60" height="34" rx="6"/><text class="t-term" x="210" y="33" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:22px">/</text>
<path class="ln" d="M210 42V52H60V62M210 52V62M210 52H360V62"/>
<rect class="bx-a" x="20" y="62" width="80" height="34" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="60" y="85" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">etc</text>
<rect class="bx-a" x="165" y="62" width="90" height="34" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="210" y="85" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">home</text>
<rect class="bx-a" x="320" y="62" width="80" height="34" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="360" y="85" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">var</text>
<path class="ln" d="M210 96V114"/>
<rect class="bx-ok" x="170" y="114" width="80" height="34" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="210" y="137" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">you</text>
<text class="t t-ok" x="262" y="137" style="font-size:15px">~ is /home/you</text>
<path class="ln" d="M210 148V158H85V168M210 158V168M210 158H335V168"/>
<rect class="bx-a" x="25" y="168" width="120" height="34" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="85" y="191" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">Documents</text>
<rect class="bx-a" x="155" y="168" width="110" height="34" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="210" y="191" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">projects</text>
<rect class="bx-info" x="280" y="168" width="110" height="34" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="335" y="191" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">notes.txt</text>
</svg><figcaption>Linux keeps everything in one upside-down tree. The top is called the root and is written <code>/</code>. Your own space is <code>/home/you</code>, nicknamed <code>~</code> (tilde). Orange boxes are folders, the blue one is a file.</figcaption></figure>
${V.like(`<p>A huge office building. <code>/</code> is the front door. Every floor, corridor and room hangs off it, and a <b>path</b> is the directions from the front door to one room: "go to home, then you, then projects".</p>`)}
${V.why(`<p>Windows gives each drive a letter, like <code>C:</code> and <code>D:</code>. Unix, the 1970s system Linux copies, chose one single tree instead. Even a USB stick appears as a folder inside it. One tree means every file has exactly one full address.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'/'],[2,'home'],[3,'/'],[2,'you'],[3,'/'],[2,'projects'],[3,'/'],[4,'site']],[
 '<b>Leading slash.</b> "Start at the front door." A path that begins with <code>/</code> is <b>absolute</b>: it means the same place wherever you are.',
 '<b>Folders on the way.</b> Walked through in order, top to bottom. A folder is also called a <b>directory</b>.',
 '<b>Separator.</b> A forward slash between names. Never a backslash on Linux.',
 '<b>Destination.</b> The folder or file you want to reach.'])}
<p><b>Watch yourself move.</b> The terminal is on top. The strip below shows where you are standing.</p>
${V.steps([
 ['You open a terminal. <b>pwd</b> (print working directory) answers "where am I?". You always start at home.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 190" role="img" aria-label="pwd prints /home/you; you are in you">
<rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="82" rx="8"/>
<text class="t-term" x="16" y="34" style="font-size:16px">$ pwd</text>
<text class="t-term t-a" x="16" y="70" style="font-size:16px">/home/you</text>
<rect class="bx" x="4" y="104" width="40" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="24" y="130" text-anchor="middle">/</text>
<rect class="bx" x="62" y="104" width="70" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="97" y="130" text-anchor="middle">home</text>
<rect class="bx-hl" x="150" y="104" width="60" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="180" y="130" text-anchor="middle">you</text>
<rect class="bx" x="228" y="104" width="100" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="278" y="130" text-anchor="middle">projects</text>
<rect class="bx" x="346" y="104" width="70" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="381" y="130" text-anchor="middle">site</text>
<path class="ln" d="M44 124H62M132 124H150M210 124H228M328 124H346"/>
${V.ic('person',165,150,30,'ic-a')}
</svg>`],
 ['<b>cd projects</b> (change directory). No slash at the start, so it is <b>relative</b>: "from where I stand, go into projects".',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 190" role="img" aria-label="cd projects; pwd prints /home/you/projects">
<rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="82" rx="8"/>
<text class="t-term" x="16" y="30" style="font-size:16px">$ cd projects</text>
<text class="t-term" x="16" y="54" style="font-size:16px">$ pwd</text>
<text class="t-term t-a" x="16" y="78" style="font-size:16px">/home/you/projects</text>
<rect class="bx" x="4" y="104" width="40" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="24" y="130" text-anchor="middle">/</text>
<rect class="bx" x="62" y="104" width="70" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="97" y="130" text-anchor="middle">home</text>
<rect class="bx" x="150" y="104" width="60" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="180" y="130" text-anchor="middle">you</text>
<rect class="bx-hl" x="228" y="104" width="100" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="278" y="130" text-anchor="middle">projects</text>
<rect class="bx" x="346" y="104" width="70" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="381" y="130" text-anchor="middle">site</text>
<path class="ln" d="M44 124H62M132 124H150M210 124H228M328 124H346"/>
${V.ic('person',263,150,30,'ic-a')}
</svg>`],
 ['<b>cd ..</b> goes up one level. Two dots always mean "the folder above this one".',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 190" role="img" aria-label="cd .. ; pwd prints /home/you">
<rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="82" rx="8"/>
<text class="t-term" x="16" y="30" style="font-size:16px">$ cd ..</text>
<text class="t-term" x="16" y="54" style="font-size:16px">$ pwd</text>
<text class="t-term t-a" x="16" y="78" style="font-size:16px">/home/you</text>
<rect class="bx" x="4" y="104" width="40" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="24" y="130" text-anchor="middle">/</text>
<rect class="bx" x="62" y="104" width="70" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="97" y="130" text-anchor="middle">home</text>
<rect class="bx-hl" x="150" y="104" width="60" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="180" y="130" text-anchor="middle">you</text>
<rect class="bx" x="228" y="104" width="100" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="278" y="130" text-anchor="middle">projects</text>
<rect class="bx" x="346" y="104" width="70" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="381" y="130" text-anchor="middle">site</text>
<path class="ln" d="M44 124H62M132 124H150M210 124H228M328 124H346"/>
${V.ic('person',165,150,30,'ic-a')}
</svg>`],
 ['An <b>absolute</b> path starts at <b>/</b>, so it works from anywhere. You jump straight to site in one go.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 190" role="img" aria-label="cd /home/you/projects/site; pwd prints that path">
<rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="82" rx="8"/>
<text class="t-term" x="16" y="30" style="font-size:16px">$ cd /home/you/projects/site</text>
<text class="t-term" x="16" y="54" style="font-size:16px">$ pwd</text>
<text class="t-term t-a" x="16" y="78" style="font-size:16px">/home/you/projects/site</text>
<rect class="bx-ok" x="4" y="104" width="40" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="24" y="130" text-anchor="middle">/</text>
<rect class="bx-ok" x="62" y="104" width="70" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="97" y="130" text-anchor="middle">home</text>
<rect class="bx-ok" x="150" y="104" width="60" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="180" y="130" text-anchor="middle">you</text>
<rect class="bx-ok" x="228" y="104" width="100" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="278" y="130" text-anchor="middle">projects</text>
<rect class="bx-hl" x="346" y="104" width="70" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="381" y="130" text-anchor="middle">site</text>
<path class="ln-ok" d="M44 124H62M132 124H150M210 124H228M328 124H346"/>
${V.ic('person',366,150,30,'ic-a')}
</svg>`],
 ['<b>cd -</b> jumps back to wherever you were last, and prints it. Lost? Plain <b>cd</b> or <b>cd ~</b> always takes you home.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 190" role="img" aria-label="cd - prints /home/you and returns you there">
<rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="82" rx="8"/>
<text class="t-term" x="16" y="34" style="font-size:16px">$ cd -</text>
<text class="t-term t-a" x="16" y="70" style="font-size:16px">/home/you</text>
<rect class="bx" x="4" y="104" width="40" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="24" y="130" text-anchor="middle">/</text>
<rect class="bx" x="62" y="104" width="70" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="97" y="130" text-anchor="middle">home</text>
<rect class="bx-hl" x="150" y="104" width="60" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="180" y="130" text-anchor="middle">you</text>
<rect class="bx" x="228" y="104" width="100" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="278" y="130" text-anchor="middle">projects</text>
<rect class="bx" x="346" y="104" width="70" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="381" y="130" text-anchor="middle">site</text>
<path class="ln" d="M44 124H62M132 124H150M210 124H228M328 124H346"/>
${V.ic('person',165,150,30,'ic-a')}
</svg>`]])}
${V.rules(V.rh('Rules: get these wrong and the command fails'),
 V.ok('cd /etc','Starts with / : absolute, works from anywhere'),V.ok('cd projects','No / : relative, starts where you are'),
 V.no('cd Projects','Names are case-sensitive: Projects and projects are different'),V.no('cd my folder','A space splits it into two words. Use "my folder"'),
 V.no('cd \\home\\you','Backslashes are Windows. Linux uses /'),
 V.rh('Conventions: what professionals do'),
 V.ok('my-site, notes.txt','Lower case, hyphens, no spaces in names'),V.ok('pwd','When in doubt, check where you are before you act'))}
${V.hook(`Slash first: from the front door. No slash: from where you stand. <code>..</code> is up, <code>~</code> is home, <code>-</code> is back.`)}
`)}

${V.card(2,'Look around','pwd and ls switch the lights on',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 196" role="img" aria-label="ls -la output in the home folder, with dot, dot dot and the hidden file .bashrc labelled">
<rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="270" height="184" rx="8"/>
<text class="t-term" x="16" y="32" style="font-size:16px">$ ls -la</text>
<text class="t-term" x="16" y="62" style="font-size:16px"><tspan class="t-a">d</tspan>rwxr-xr-x  .</text>
<text class="t-term" x="16" y="88" style="font-size:16px"><tspan class="t-a">d</tspan>rwxr-xr-x  ..</text>
<text class="t-term" x="16" y="114" style="font-size:16px">-rw-r--r--  .bashrc</text>
<text class="t-term" x="16" y="140" style="font-size:16px"><tspan class="t-a">d</tspan>rwxr-xr-x  Documents</text>
<text class="t-term" x="16" y="166" style="font-size:16px">-rw-r--r--  notes.txt</text>
<path class="ln-d" d="M232 57H286M232 83H286M240 109H286"/>
<text class="t" x="292" y="62">this folder</text>
<text class="t" x="292" y="88">the one above</text>
<text class="t t-a" x="292" y="114">hidden file</text>
<text class="t" x="292" y="140"><tspan class="t-a" style="font-weight:700">d</tspan> = directory</text>
<text class="t" x="292" y="166">- = file</text>
</svg><figcaption>A shortened <code>ls -la</code>. Names that start with a dot are hidden from a plain <code>ls</code>. The first letter of each line says what it is. The other nine letters are permissions, which is the next lesson.</figcaption></figure>
${V.like(`<p>Walking into a dark room. <code>pwd</code> tells you which room you are in; <code>ls</code> switches the light on. <code>-a</code> also opens the drawers where the hidden things are kept.</p>`)}
${V.why(`<p>A terminal shows nothing until you ask, so "where am I?" and "what is here?" are the two questions you ask most. Hidden <b>dotfiles</b> such as <code>.bashrc</code> hold settings. They are hidden so they don't clutter your view, not because they are secret.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'ls'],' ',[2,'-l'],[3,'a'],' ',[4,'~/projects']],[
 '<b>Command.</b> <code>ls</code> lists what is in a folder.',
 '<b>-l (long).</b> One item per line with details: type, permissions, owner, size, date.',
 '<b>a (all).</b> Include hidden dotfiles. Short flags can be squashed together: <code>-la</code> is <code>-l -a</code>.',
 '<b>Where (optional).</b> Leave it out and ls lists the folder you are in.'])}
${V.rules(V.ok('ls -la','Space between the command and its flags'),V.no('ls-la','No space: Linux looks for a command called "ls-la"'),
 V.no('LS','Commands are lower case'),V.ok('tree','Draws the folders below you as a tree (may need installing on a real machine)'))}
${V.hook(`<code>pwd</code>: where am I? <code>ls -la</code>: what is here, even the hidden things?`)}
`)}

${V.card(3,'Make, copy, move, delete','five verbs that shape the tree',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 150" role="img" aria-label="Five commands as pictures: mkdir makes a folder, touch makes a file, cp copies, mv moves or renames, rm deletes">
${V.ic('folder',18,10,48,'ic-a')}${V.ic('file',100,10,48,'ic-info')}${V.ic('file',178,10,40,'ic-ok')}${V.ic('file',194,24,40,'ic-ok')}${V.ic('arrow',266,14,44,'ic-a')}${V.ic('cross',348,10,48,'ic-bad')}
<text class="t-m" x="42" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">mkdir</text>
<text class="t-m" x="124" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">touch</text>
<text class="t-m" x="208" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">cp</text>
<text class="t-m" x="290" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">mv</text>
<text class="t-m" x="372" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">rm</text>
<text class="t" x="42" y="126" text-anchor="middle">new folder</text>
<text class="t" x="124" y="126" text-anchor="middle">new file</text>
<text class="t" x="208" y="126" text-anchor="middle">copy</text>
<text class="t" x="290" y="126" text-anchor="middle">move or</text>
<text class="t" x="290" y="144" text-anchor="middle">rename</text>
<text class="t t-bad" x="372" y="126" text-anchor="middle">delete</text>
<text class="t t-bad" x="372" y="144" text-anchor="middle">forever</text>
</svg><figcaption>The five verbs. Each is short for an English word: make directory, touch (create an empty file), copy, move, remove.</figcaption></figure>
${V.like(`<p><code>cp</code> is a photocopier: you end up with two. <code>mv</code> is picking a box up and putting it somewhere else; giving it a new label is just a move to a new name. <code>rm</code> is a shredder, and there is no recycle bin to rescue you.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'mkdir'],' ',[2,'-p'],' ',[3,'projects/site/css']],[
 '<b>Command.</b> Make a directory.',
 '<b>-p (parents).</b> Also create any missing folders on the way. Without it, mkdir fails if <code>projects</code> doesn\'t exist yet.',
 '<b>Path.</b> Relative here, so it is built inside the folder you are in.'])}
${V.steps([
 ['<b>mkdir -p</b> builds three folders in one go, one inside the next.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 236" role="img" aria-label="mkdir -p creates projects, site and css">
<rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="40" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="32" style="font-size:16px">$ mkdir -p projects/site/css</text>
<rect class="bx" x="6" y="62" width="128" height="70" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="16" y="84">~</text><text class="t-m" x="22" y="114">notes.txt</text>
<text class="t-m t-ok" x="160" y="82" style="font-size:16px">projects/</text>
<text class="t-m t-ok" x="184" y="110" style="font-size:16px">site/</text>
<text class="t-m t-ok" x="208" y="138" style="font-size:16px">css/</text>
</svg>`],
 ['Inside site, <b>touch</b> creates two empty files. Note <b>css/style.css</b>: a relative path into the css folder.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 236" role="img" aria-label="touch creates index.html and css/style.css">
<rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="40" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="32" style="font-size:16px">$ touch index.html css/style.css</text>
<rect class="bx" x="6" y="62" width="128" height="70" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="16" y="84">~</text><text class="t-m" x="22" y="114">notes.txt</text>
<text class="t-m" x="160" y="82" style="font-size:16px">projects/</text>
<text class="t-m" x="184" y="110" style="font-size:16px">site/</text>
<text class="t-m" x="208" y="138" style="font-size:16px">css/</text>
<text class="t-m t-ok" x="232" y="166" style="font-size:16px">style.css</text>
<text class="t-m t-ok" x="208" y="194" style="font-size:16px">index.html</text>
</svg>`],
 ['<b>cp ~/notes.txt .</b> copies the notes here. The lone dot means "this folder". The original stays at home.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 236" role="img" aria-label="cp makes a copy of notes.txt inside site">
<rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="40" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="32" style="font-size:16px">$ cp ~/notes.txt .</text>
<rect class="bx-hl" x="6" y="62" width="128" height="70" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="16" y="84">~</text><text class="t-m" x="22" y="114">notes.txt</text>
<text class="t-m" x="160" y="82" style="font-size:16px">projects/</text>
<text class="t-m" x="184" y="110" style="font-size:16px">site/</text>
<text class="t-m" x="208" y="138" style="font-size:16px">css/</text>
<text class="t-m" x="232" y="166" style="font-size:16px">style.css</text>
<text class="t-m" x="208" y="194" style="font-size:16px">index.html</text>
<text class="t-m t-ok" x="208" y="222" style="font-size:16px">notes.txt</text>
<path class="ln-ok" d="M70 132C80 200 130 218 192 217"/><polygon class="ah-ok" points="190,210 202,217 190,224"/>
</svg>`],
 ['<b>mv notes.txt README.md</b> renames it. Same file, new label. Check the shape any time with <b>tree</b>.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 236" role="img" aria-label="mv renames notes.txt to README.md">
<rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="40" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="32" style="font-size:16px">$ mv notes.txt README.md</text>
<rect class="bx" x="6" y="62" width="128" height="70" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="16" y="84">~</text><text class="t-m" x="22" y="114">notes.txt</text>
<text class="t-m" x="160" y="82" style="font-size:16px">projects/</text>
<text class="t-m" x="184" y="110" style="font-size:16px">site/</text>
<text class="t-m" x="208" y="138" style="font-size:16px">css/</text>
<text class="t-m" x="232" y="166" style="font-size:16px">style.css</text>
<text class="t-m" x="208" y="194" style="font-size:16px">index.html</text>
<text class="t-m t-a" x="208" y="222" style="font-size:16px">README.md</text>
</svg>`]])}
${V.rules(V.rh('Rules: these bite'),
 V.no('rm notes.txt','Gone at once. No bin, no undo. Read the line twice before Enter'),V.ok('rm -r old-dir','Folders need -r (recursive) to delete them and everything inside'),
 V.ok('cp -r src backup','Copying a folder also needs -r'),V.no('mv a.txt b.txt','If b.txt already exists, it is silently replaced. Add -i to be asked first'),
 V.rh('Conventions'),
 V.ok('mkdir -p','Safe to repeat: no error if the folders already exist'),V.ok('ls before rm','Look at what you are about to delete'))}
${V.build(`<ol><li>Check where you are with <code>pwd</code> and list everything, hidden files included.</li><li>Build a nested folder path in one command with <code>-p</code>, then <code>cd</code> into the middle folder.</li><li>Create two empty files with <code>touch</code>, one of them inside the sub-folder.</li><li>Copy a file from home with <code>~</code> and <code>.</code>, then rename the copy with <code>mv</code>.</li><li>Run <code>tree</code> to check, then go home.</li></ol>`)}
${V.hook(`Make, touch, copy, move, remove. And <code>rm</code> never asks twice.`)}
`)}

<div class="try"><b>Try it in your head</b>1. You are in <code>/home/you/projects</code>. Where does <code>cd ..</code> take you? <i>/home/you.</i> 2. Is <code>projects/site</code> absolute or relative? <i>Relative: it doesn't start with /.</i> 3. Which command shows <code>.bashrc</code>: <code>ls</code> or <code>ls -a</code>? <i>ls -a.</i></div>
`);

explain('l2',`
<p>Every file on a Linux computer carries a tiny lock that says who may open it, change it or run it. Get it wrong and your script won't start, or worse, your passwords are readable by everyone. Get it right and you can read any <code>ls -l</code> line, and any number like 755, at a glance.</p>

${V.card(1,'Owner, group, others','three sets of keys',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 214" role="img" aria-label="deploy.sh gives three sets of keys: the owner gets r w x, the group gets r and x, everyone else gets r and x">
${V.ic('person',44,4,52,'ic-a')}${V.ic('people',184,4,52,'ic-info')}${V.ic('globe',324,4,52,'ic-ok')}
<text class="t-b" x="70" y="84" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">Owner (u)</text>
<text class="t-b" x="210" y="84" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">Group (g)</text>
<text class="t-b" x="350" y="84" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">Others (o)</text>
<rect class="bx-a" x="13" y="100" width="34" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="30" y="127" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:20px;font-weight:700">r</text><rect class="bx-a" x="53" y="100" width="34" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="70" y="127" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:20px;font-weight:700">w</text><rect class="bx-a" x="93" y="100" width="34" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="110" y="127" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:20px;font-weight:700">x</text><rect class="bx-info" x="153" y="100" width="34" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="170" y="127" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:20px;font-weight:700">r</text><rect class="ln-d" x="193" y="100" width="34" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="210" y="127" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:20px">-</text><rect class="bx-info" x="233" y="100" width="34" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="250" y="127" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:20px;font-weight:700">x</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="293" y="100" width="34" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="310" y="127" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:20px;font-weight:700">r</text><rect class="ln-d" x="333" y="100" width="34" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="350" y="127" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:20px">-</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="373" y="100" width="34" height="40" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="390" y="127" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:20px;font-weight:700">x</text>
<path class="ln-d" d="M140 70V150M280 70V150"/>
<text class="t-m" x="210" y="196" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:24px">-<tspan class="t-a">rwx</tspan><tspan class="t-info">r-x</tspan><tspan class="t-ok">r-x</tspan></text>
</svg><figcaption>Every file hands out three sets of keys. The owner is one person. The group is a named team of users. Others is everybody else. <code>r</code>, <code>w</code> and <code>x</code> are the keys; a dash means that key is missing. Read left to right, the nine letters are exactly what <code>ls -l</code> prints.</figcaption></figure>
${V.like(`<p>Think of a house. The <b>owner</b> has a full set of keys. The <b>family</b> (the group) gets some keys. A <b>stranger</b> walking past (others) gets maybe one key, or none. Every file keeps a little card that says exactly which keys each of the three gets.</p>`)}
${V.why(`<p>Unix, the system Linux grew from, was built in the 1970s for one big computer shared by dozens of people at once. Without locks, anyone could read your work or delete the system by accident. So every file got an <b>owner</b> (one user), a <b>group</b> (a named team of users) and nine on/off switches. Type <code>whoami</code> to see your user name and <code>groups</code> to see the teams you belong to.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'-'],[2,'rwx'],[3,'r-x'],[4,'r-x'],' 1 ',[5,'you you'],'  48 Oct  9 10:30 ',[6,'deploy.sh']],[
 '<b>Type.</b> <code>-</code> is a normal file, <code>d</code> is a directory (folder).',
 '<b>Owner keys.</b> What the owner may do: here read, write and execute.',
 '<b>Group keys.</b> What members of the file\'s group may do: read and execute, no write.',
 '<b>Others keys.</b> What everybody else may do.',
 '<b>Owner, then group.</b> The file belongs to the user <code>you</code> and the group <code>you</code>. Many Linux systems give each user a private group with the same name.',
 '<b>File name.</b> The 1, the size (48 bytes) and the date are not about permissions.'])}
<p><b>How Linux decides.</b> Every time someone opens, saves or runs a file, Linux walks through three gates in a fixed order. Watch it.</p>
${V.steps([
 ['Meet <b>report.txt</b>. Owner <b>ada</b> may read and write. Members of the group <b>devs</b> may only read. Everyone else gets nothing. Now three people knock.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 242" role="img" aria-label="report.txt: owner ada rw-, group devs r--, others none"><text class="t-m" x="210" y="26" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">-<tspan class="t-a">rw-</tspan><tspan class="t-info">r--</tspan><tspan class="t-ok">---</tspan> ada devs report.txt</text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="42" width="130" height="72" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:14px">1 Owner: ada</text><text class="t-m t-a" x="71" y="100" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700">rw-</text><rect class="bx" x="145" y="42" width="130" height="72" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="155" y="66" style="font-size:14px">2 Group: devs</text><text class="t-m t-info" x="210" y="100" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700">r--</text><rect class="bx" x="284" y="42" width="130" height="72" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="294" y="66" style="font-size:14px">3 Others</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="349" y="100" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700">---</text><text class="t" x="10" y="152" style="font-size:16px">Checked in order: gate 1, then 2, then 3.</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>ada</b> wants to write. Gate 1: is she the owner? Yes. So Linux uses the owner keys, <b>rw-</b>. The w key is there: allowed.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 242" role="img" aria-label="ada is the owner, owner keys include w, allowed"><text class="t-m" x="210" y="26" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">-<tspan class="t-a">rw-</tspan><tspan class="t-info">r--</tspan><tspan class="t-ok">---</tspan> ada devs report.txt</text><rect class="bx-hl" x="6" y="42" width="130" height="72" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:14px">1 Owner: ada</text><text class="t-m t-a" x="71" y="100" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700">rw-</text><text class="t-b t-ok" x="128" y="100" text-anchor="end" style="font-size:16px">yes</text><rect class="bx" x="145" y="42" width="130" height="72" rx="8"/><text class="t-b t-dim" x="155" y="66" style="font-size:14px">2 Group: devs</text><text class="t-m t-info t-dim" x="210" y="100" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700">r--</text><rect class="bx" x="284" y="42" width="130" height="72" rx="8"/><text class="t-b t-dim" x="294" y="66" style="font-size:14px">3 Others</text><text class="t-m t-ok t-dim" x="349" y="100" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700">---</text>${V.ic('person',8,124,44,'ic-a')}<text class="t-b" x="62" y="152" style="font-size:17px">ada <tspan class="t-a">wants to WRITE</tspan></text><text class="t" x="10" y="190" style="font-size:15px">Is ada the owner? Yes. Use rw-. Is w there? Yes.</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="202" width="408" height="34" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="210" y="225" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">Allowed</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>bob</b> is in the devs group and wants to read. Gate 1: owner? No. Gate 2: in devs? Yes, so the group keys <b>r--</b> apply. r is there: allowed.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 242" role="img" aria-label="bob is in devs, group keys include r, allowed"><text class="t-m" x="210" y="26" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">-<tspan class="t-a">rw-</tspan><tspan class="t-info">r--</tspan><tspan class="t-ok">---</tspan> ada devs report.txt</text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="42" width="130" height="72" rx="8"/><text class="t-b t-dim" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:14px">1 Owner: ada</text><text class="t-m t-a t-dim" x="71" y="100" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700">rw-</text><text class="t-b t-bad" x="128" y="100" text-anchor="end" style="font-size:16px">no</text><rect class="bx-hl" x="145" y="42" width="130" height="72" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="155" y="66" style="font-size:14px">2 Group: devs</text><text class="t-m t-info" x="210" y="100" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700">r--</text><text class="t-b t-ok" x="267" y="100" text-anchor="end" style="font-size:16px">yes</text><rect class="bx" x="284" y="42" width="130" height="72" rx="8"/><text class="t-b t-dim" x="294" y="66" style="font-size:14px">3 Others</text><text class="t-m t-ok t-dim" x="349" y="100" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700">---</text>${V.ic('people',8,124,44,'ic-a')}<text class="t-b" x="62" y="152" style="font-size:17px">bob <tspan class="t-a">wants to READ</tspan></text><text class="t" x="10" y="190" style="font-size:15px">Owner? No. In devs? Yes. Use r--. Is r there? Yes.</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="202" width="408" height="34" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="210" y="225" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">Allowed</text></svg>`],
 ['Now <b>bob</b> wants to write. He still matches gate 2, and r-- has no w. Denied. Linux stops at the <b>first</b> gate that matches; it never moves on to try another.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 242" role="img" aria-label="bob matches the group, r-- has no w, permission denied"><text class="t-m" x="210" y="26" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">-<tspan class="t-a">rw-</tspan><tspan class="t-info">r--</tspan><tspan class="t-ok">---</tspan> ada devs report.txt</text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="42" width="130" height="72" rx="8"/><text class="t-b t-dim" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:14px">1 Owner: ada</text><text class="t-m t-a t-dim" x="71" y="100" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700">rw-</text><text class="t-b t-bad" x="128" y="100" text-anchor="end" style="font-size:16px">no</text><rect class="bx-hl" x="145" y="42" width="130" height="72" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="155" y="66" style="font-size:14px">2 Group: devs</text><text class="t-m t-info" x="210" y="100" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700">r--</text><text class="t-b t-ok" x="267" y="100" text-anchor="end" style="font-size:16px">yes</text><rect class="bx" x="284" y="42" width="130" height="72" rx="8"/><text class="t-b t-dim" x="294" y="66" style="font-size:14px">3 Others</text><text class="t-m t-ok t-dim" x="349" y="100" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700">---</text>${V.ic('people',8,124,44,'ic-a')}<text class="t-b" x="62" y="152" style="font-size:17px">bob <tspan class="t-a">wants to WRITE</tspan></text><text class="t" x="10" y="190" style="font-size:15px">Owner? No. In devs? Yes. Use r--. Is w there? No.</text><rect class="bx-bad" x="6" y="202" width="408" height="34" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="210" y="225" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">Permission denied</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>carol</b> is not the owner and not in devs, so she falls through to gate 3, where there are no keys at all. (Only root, coming up in card 4, can walk past every gate.)',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 242" role="img" aria-label="carol is neither owner nor group, others has no keys, permission denied"><text class="t-m" x="210" y="26" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">-<tspan class="t-a">rw-</tspan><tspan class="t-info">r--</tspan><tspan class="t-ok">---</tspan> ada devs report.txt</text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="42" width="130" height="72" rx="8"/><text class="t-b t-dim" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:14px">1 Owner: ada</text><text class="t-m t-a t-dim" x="71" y="100" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700">rw-</text><text class="t-b t-bad" x="128" y="100" text-anchor="end" style="font-size:16px">no</text><rect class="bx" x="145" y="42" width="130" height="72" rx="8"/><text class="t-b t-dim" x="155" y="66" style="font-size:14px">2 Group: devs</text><text class="t-m t-info t-dim" x="210" y="100" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700">r--</text><text class="t-b t-bad" x="267" y="100" text-anchor="end" style="font-size:16px">no</text><rect class="bx-hl" x="284" y="42" width="130" height="72" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="294" y="66" style="font-size:14px">3 Others</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="349" y="100" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700">---</text><text class="t-b t-ok" x="406" y="100" text-anchor="end" style="font-size:16px">yes</text>${V.ic('globe',8,124,44,'ic-a')}<text class="t-b" x="62" y="152" style="font-size:17px">carol <tspan class="t-a">wants to READ</tspan></text><text class="t" x="10" y="190" style="font-size:15px">Owner? No. In devs? No. Use ---. Is r there? No.</text><rect class="bx-bad" x="6" y="202" width="408" height="34" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="210" y="225" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">Permission denied</text></svg>`]])}
${V.rules(V.rh('Rules: how the check really works'),
 V.ok('owner, then group, then others','Checked in that order. The first gate you match is the only one used'),
 V.no('"others has r, so I can read"','Not if you are the owner and the owner set has no r. You never fall through'),
 V.ok('Permission denied','Means your matching set lacks the key you needed'))}
${V.hook(`Three sets of keys: <b>u</b>ser (the owner), <b>g</b>roup, <b>o</b>thers. Linux tries them in that order and stops at the first one that fits.`)}
`)}

${V.card(2,'r, w, x and the numbers','three switches worth 4, 2 and 1',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 206" role="img" aria-label="Three light switches worth 4, 2 and 1. Read and execute are on, write is off, so the digit is 5"><rect class="bx-ok" x="14" y="46" width="90" height="96" rx="12"/><rect class="bx-dark" x="44" y="58" width="30" height="32" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="59" y="30" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:24px;font-weight:700">r</text><text class="t-b t-ok" x="59" y="168" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">ON = 4</text><text class="t" x="59" y="194" text-anchor="middle">read: 4</text><rect class="bx" x="122" y="46" width="90" height="96" rx="12"/><rect class="bx-dark" x="152" y="98" width="30" height="32" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="167" y="30" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:24px;font-weight:700">w</text><text class="t-b" x="167" y="168" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">off = 0</text><text class="t" x="167" y="194" text-anchor="middle">write: 2</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="230" y="46" width="90" height="96" rx="12"/><rect class="bx-dark" x="260" y="58" width="30" height="32" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="275" y="30" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:24px;font-weight:700">x</text><text class="t-b t-ok" x="275" y="168" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">ON = 1</text><text class="t" x="275" y="194" text-anchor="middle">execute: 1</text><text class="t-m" x="378" y="96" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">4+0+1</text><text class="t-m t-a" x="378" y="140" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:40px;font-weight:700">5</text><text class="t" x="378" y="168" text-anchor="middle">r-x</text></svg><figcaption>One set of keys is a panel of three switches worth 4, 2 and 1. Add up the switches that are on and you get one digit. Here read and execute are on: 4 + 1 = 5, written <code>r-x</code>.</figcaption></figure>
${V.like(`<p>Each set of keys is a little panel of three light switches. The <b>read</b> switch is worth 4, <b>write</b> is worth 2, <b>execute</b> is worth 1. Add up the switches that are on and you get one digit from 0 to 7. Three panels (owner, group, others) give three digits, like 755.</p>`)}
${V.why(`<p>The computer stores each switch as one bit, a 1 or a 0. Three bits can count from 0 to 7, so each set fits in one digit, and the whole lock fits in three digits. That is far quicker to type than nine letters, which is why every tutorial and server guide uses numbers.</p>`)}
<div class="tbl-wrap"><table><tr><th>Key</th><th>On a file</th><th>On a folder</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>r</code> = 4</td><td>Open it and see what is inside</td><td>List the names in it (<code>ls</code>)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>w</code> = 2</td><td>Change or empty it</td><td>Create, rename or delete files in it</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>x</code> = 1</td><td>Run it as a program</td><td>Go into it (<code>cd</code>)</td></tr></table></div>
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 148" role="img" aria-label="All eight digits: 0 none, 1 x, 2 w, 3 wx, 4 r, 5 rx, 6 rw, 7 rwx"><rect class="bx-bad" x="8" y="8" width="96" height="62" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="34" y="48" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:26px;font-weight:700">0</text><text class="t-m" x="74" y="47" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">---</text><rect class="bx" x="110" y="8" width="96" height="62" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="136" y="48" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:26px;font-weight:700">1</text><text class="t-m" x="176" y="47" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">--x</text><rect class="bx" x="212" y="8" width="96" height="62" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="238" y="48" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:26px;font-weight:700">2</text><text class="t-m" x="278" y="47" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">-w-</text><rect class="bx" x="314" y="8" width="96" height="62" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="340" y="48" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:26px;font-weight:700">3</text><text class="t-m" x="380" y="47" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">-wx</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="8" y="78" width="96" height="62" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="34" y="118" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:26px;font-weight:700">4</text><text class="t-m" x="74" y="117" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">r--</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="110" y="78" width="96" height="62" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="136" y="118" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:26px;font-weight:700">5</text><text class="t-m" x="176" y="117" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">r-x</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="212" y="78" width="96" height="62" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="238" y="118" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:26px;font-weight:700">6</text><text class="t-m" x="278" y="117" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">rw-</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="314" y="78" width="96" height="62" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="340" y="118" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:26px;font-weight:700">7</text><text class="t-m" x="380" y="117" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">rwx</text></svg><figcaption>Every possible digit. Only eight exist, because three switches can only make the totals 0 to 7. The green ones are the ones you will meet most: 7, 6, 5, 4 and 0.</figcaption></figure>
${V.anat([[1,'chmod'],' ',[2,'7'],[3,'5'],[4,'5'],' ',[5,'deploy.sh']],[
 '<b>chmod.</b> "Change mode": rewrite the lock on a file.',
 '<b>Owner digit.</b> 7 = 4 + 2 + 1, so rwx.',
 '<b>Group digit.</b> 5 = 4 + 1, so r-x.',
 '<b>Others digit.</b> 5 again, r-x. The order of the digits never changes: owner, group, others.',
 '<b>File.</b> The file whose lock you are changing.'])}
<p><b>Watch 755 being decoded.</b> Each digit is unpacked into its three switches.</p>
${V.steps([
 ['Three digits, three sets of keys, always in the same order: <b>owner, group, others</b>. First digit: <b>7</b>. Which switches add up to 7? All three: 4 + 2 + 1. So the owner gets <b>rwx</b>.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 228" role="img" aria-label="7 is 4 plus 2 plus 1, rwx for the owner"><rect class="bx-hl" x="36" y="8" width="68" height="54" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="70" y="50" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:38px;font-weight:700">7</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="8" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="27" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">4</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="27" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">r</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="52" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="71" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">2</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="71" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">w</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="96" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="115" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">1</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="115" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">x</text><text class="t-m" x="70" y="160" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">4+2+1 = 7</text><text class="t-m t-a" x="70" y="192" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:24px;font-weight:700">rwx</text><text class="t-b" x="70" y="218" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">owner</text><text class="t-m t-dim" x="210" y="50" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:38px;font-weight:700">5</text><rect class="bx" x="148" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m t-dim" x="167" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">4</text><text class="t-m t-dim" x="167" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">r</text><rect class="bx" x="192" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m t-dim" x="211" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">2</text><text class="t-m t-dim" x="211" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">w</text><rect class="bx" x="236" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m t-dim" x="255" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">1</text><text class="t-m t-dim" x="255" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">x</text><text class="t-b t-dim" x="210" y="218" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">group</text><text class="t-m t-dim" x="350" y="50" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:38px;font-weight:700">5</text><rect class="bx" x="288" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m t-dim" x="307" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">4</text><text class="t-m t-dim" x="307" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">r</text><rect class="bx" x="332" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m t-dim" x="351" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">2</text><text class="t-m t-dim" x="351" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">w</text><rect class="bx" x="376" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m t-dim" x="395" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">1</text><text class="t-m t-dim" x="395" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">x</text><text class="t-b t-dim" x="350" y="218" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">others</text></svg>`],
 ['Second digit: <b>5</b>. 4 + 1 = 5, so read and execute are on and write is off. The group gets <b>r-x</b>.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 228" role="img" aria-label="5 is 4 plus 1, r-x for the group"><text class="t-m" x="70" y="50" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:38px;font-weight:700">7</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="8" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="27" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">4</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="27" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">r</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="52" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="71" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">2</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="71" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">w</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="96" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="115" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">1</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="115" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">x</text><text class="t-m" x="70" y="160" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">4+2+1 = 7</text><text class="t-m t-a" x="70" y="192" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:24px;font-weight:700">rwx</text><text class="t-b" x="70" y="218" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">owner</text><rect class="bx-hl" x="176" y="8" width="68" height="54" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="210" y="50" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:38px;font-weight:700">5</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="148" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="167" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">4</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="167" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">r</text><rect class="bx" x="192" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m t-dim" x="211" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">2</text><text class="t-m t-dim" x="211" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">w</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="236" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="255" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">1</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="255" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">x</text><text class="t-m" x="210" y="160" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">4+0+1 = 5</text><text class="t-m t-a" x="210" y="192" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:24px;font-weight:700">r-x</text><text class="t-b" x="210" y="218" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">group</text><text class="t-m t-dim" x="350" y="50" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:38px;font-weight:700">5</text><rect class="bx" x="288" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m t-dim" x="307" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">4</text><text class="t-m t-dim" x="307" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">r</text><rect class="bx" x="332" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m t-dim" x="351" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">2</text><text class="t-m t-dim" x="351" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">w</text><rect class="bx" x="376" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m t-dim" x="395" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">1</text><text class="t-m t-dim" x="395" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">x</text><text class="t-b t-dim" x="350" y="218" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">others</text></svg>`],
 ['Third digit: <b>5</b> again, so others also get <b>r-x</b>.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 228" role="img" aria-label="5 is 4 plus 1, r-x for others"><text class="t-m" x="70" y="50" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:38px;font-weight:700">7</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="8" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="27" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">4</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="27" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">r</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="52" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="71" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">2</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="71" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">w</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="96" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="115" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">1</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="115" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">x</text><text class="t-m" x="70" y="160" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">4+2+1 = 7</text><text class="t-m t-a" x="70" y="192" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:24px;font-weight:700">rwx</text><text class="t-b" x="70" y="218" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">owner</text><text class="t-m" x="210" y="50" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:38px;font-weight:700">5</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="148" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="167" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">4</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="167" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">r</text><rect class="bx" x="192" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m t-dim" x="211" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">2</text><text class="t-m t-dim" x="211" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">w</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="236" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="255" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">1</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="255" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">x</text><text class="t-m" x="210" y="160" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">4+0+1 = 5</text><text class="t-m t-a" x="210" y="192" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:24px;font-weight:700">r-x</text><text class="t-b" x="210" y="218" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">group</text><rect class="bx-hl" x="316" y="8" width="68" height="54" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="350" y="50" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:38px;font-weight:700">5</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="288" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="307" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">4</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="307" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">r</text><rect class="bx" x="332" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m t-dim" x="351" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">2</text><text class="t-m t-dim" x="351" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">w</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="376" y="74" width="38" height="36" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="395" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">1</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="395" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">x</text><text class="t-m" x="350" y="160" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">4+0+1 = 5</text><text class="t-m t-a" x="350" y="192" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:24px;font-weight:700">r-x</text><text class="t-b" x="350" y="218" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">others</text></svg>`],
 ['Put the three together and <b>755</b> is <b>rwxr-xr-x</b>: the classic setting for scripts and folders.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 228" role="img" aria-label="755 becomes rwxr-xr-x"><text class="t-m" x="70" y="50" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:38px;font-weight:700">7</text><text class="t-m t-a" x="70" y="96" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:24px;font-weight:700">rwx</text><text class="t-b" x="70" y="124" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">owner</text><text class="t-m" x="210" y="50" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:38px;font-weight:700">5</text><text class="t-m t-a" x="210" y="96" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:24px;font-weight:700">r-x</text><text class="t-b" x="210" y="124" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">group</text><text class="t-m" x="350" y="50" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:38px;font-weight:700">5</text><text class="t-m t-a" x="350" y="96" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:24px;font-weight:700">r-x</text><text class="t-b" x="350" y="124" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">others</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="142" width="408" height="78" rx="10"/><text class="t-m" x="210" y="176" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:26px;font-weight:700">-rwxr-xr-x</text><text class="t" x="210" y="206" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">You edit and run it. Others read and run it.</text></svg>`]])}
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" role="img" aria-label="755 for scripts and folders, 644 for normal files, 600 for secrets"><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="6" width="408" height="58" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="22" y="44" style="font-size:26px;font-weight:700">755</text><text class="t-m t-a" x="96" y="43" style="font-size:19px">rwxr-xr-x</text><text class="t-b" x="226" y="31" style="font-size:15px">Scripts and folders</text><text class="t" x="226" y="53" style="font-size:14px">all can read and run it</text><rect class="bx-info" x="6" y="72" width="408" height="58" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="22" y="110" style="font-size:26px;font-weight:700">644</text><text class="t-m t-a" x="96" y="109" style="font-size:19px">rw-r--r--</text><text class="t-b" x="226" y="97" style="font-size:15px">Normal files</text><text class="t" x="226" y="119" style="font-size:14px">all read, only you write</text><rect class="bx-warn" x="6" y="138" width="408" height="58" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="22" y="176" style="font-size:26px;font-weight:700">600</text><text class="t-m t-a" x="96" y="175" style="font-size:19px">rw-------</text><text class="t-b" x="226" y="163" style="font-size:15px">Secrets, SSH keys</text><text class="t" x="226" y="185" style="font-size:14px">only you, nobody else</text></svg><figcaption>The three numbers you will type for years. Read each one digit by digit: 6 is 4 + 2 (read and write), 4 is read only, 0 is nothing.</figcaption></figure>
${V.rules(V.rh('Rules: get these wrong and things break or leak'),
 V.no('chmod 777 file','Everyone on the machine can change it. Never the fix for "Permission denied"'),
 V.ok('chmod 600 ~/.ssh/id_ed25519','SSH refuses private keys that anyone else can read'),
 V.no('chmod 644 folder/','Without x nobody can cd into the folder. Folders want 755'),
 V.ok('chmod 755 deploy.sh','Scripts need x to run'),
 V.rh('Conventions: the professional defaults'),
 V.ok('644','Ordinary files: web pages, code, images'),V.ok('755','Scripts and folders'),V.ok('600','Secrets: .env files, keys, passwords'))}
${V.build(`<ol><li>Say who needs what in words: "I read and write; nobody else gets anything."</li><li>Owner: read + write = 4 + 2 = <b>6</b>.</li><li>Group: nothing = <b>0</b>. Others: nothing = <b>0</b>.</li><li>Write the digits in order: <code>chmod 600 file</code>.</li><li>Check with <code>ls -l</code>: you should see <code>-rw-------</code>.</li></ol>`)}
${V.hook(`Read 4, write 2, run 1. Add them up per person, in the order owner, group, others. 7 is everything, 0 is nothing.`)}
`)}

${V.card(3,'chmod in action','fixing "Permission denied"',`
${V.anat([[1,'chmod'],' ',[2,'u'],[3,'+'],[4,'x'],' ',[5,'deploy.sh']],[
 '<b>chmod.</b> The same command, used with letters instead of digits.',
 '<b>Who.</b> <code>u</code> owner (user), <code>g</code> group, <code>o</code> others, <code>a</code> all. Leave it out and it means all (minus anything your system blocks by default).',
 '<b>How.</b> <code>+</code> switches on, <code>-</code> switches off, <code>=</code> sets exactly.',
 '<b>Which key.</b> <code>r</code>, <code>w</code> or <code>x</code>, or several: <code>g+rw</code>.',
 '<b>File.</b>'])}
${V.like(`<p>Digits are like replacing the whole lock; letters are like adding or removing one key. <code>chmod 600</code> rebuilds all nine switches. <code>chmod +x</code> flips one switch and leaves the rest alone.</p>`)}
${V.steps([
 ['You try to run the script. Bash refuses. <b>ls -l</b> shows why: there is no <b>x</b> anywhere, not even for you.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 176" role="img" aria-label="Permission denied, no x anywhere"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="164" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ ./deploy.sh</text><text class="t-term t-bad" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">bash: ./deploy.sh: Permission denied</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ ls -l deploy.sh</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="126" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">-<tspan class="t-a">rw-</tspan><tspan class="t-info">r--</tspan><tspan class="t-ok">r--</tspan> you you 48 deploy.sh</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>chmod +x</b> flips the x switch on. With no letter in front, it is added for all three sets, so 644 becomes 755.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 176" role="img" aria-label="chmod +x adds x for all three sets"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="164" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ chmod +x deploy.sh</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ ls -l deploy.sh</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">-<tspan class="t-a">rwx</tspan><tspan class="t-info">r-x</tspan><tspan class="t-ok">r-x</tspan> you you 48 deploy.sh</text></svg>`],
 ['Run it again. This time Linux finds the x key in your set and lets the script start.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 176" role="img" aria-label="The script runs"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="164" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ ./deploy.sh</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">Deploying the app...</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">Done!</text></svg>`],
 ['Now the secrets file. <b>chmod 600</b> sets all nine switches at once: 6 (rw-) for you, 0 for the group, 0 for others.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 176" role="img" aria-label="chmod 600 locks secrets.env to the owner"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="164" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ chmod 600 secrets.env</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ ls -l secrets.env</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">-<tspan class="t-a">rw-</tspan><tspan class="t-info">---</tspan><tspan class="t-ok">---</tspan> you you 23 secrets.env</text></svg>`]])}
${V.rules(V.ok('./deploy.sh','Run a script in this folder with ./ in front'),V.no('deploy.sh','Without ./ the shell only looks in the standard program folders'),
 V.ok('chmod +x then ./run','The x key is needed before a script will start'),V.no('sudo ./deploy.sh','sudo does not fix a missing x. It just runs things as root'))}
${V.hook(`Digits replace the whole lock. Letters add or remove one key.`)}
`)}

${V.card(4,'root and sudo','borrowing the master key',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 180" role="img" aria-label="You hold your own keys. sudo lends you root's master key for one command, then takes it back">
${V.ic('person',22,20,60,'ic-a')}<text class="t-b" x="52" y="104" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">you</text><text class="t" x="52" y="126" text-anchor="middle">your own keys</text>
<rect class="bx-warn" x="132" y="34" width="156" height="58" rx="10"/><text class="t-m" x="210" y="70" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700">sudo</text>
<path class="ln-a" d="M90 62H124"/><polygon class="ah-a" points="122,55 122,69 132,62"/>
<path class="ln-a" d="M288 62H322"/><polygon class="ah-a" points="320,55 320,69 330,62"/>
${V.ic('key',336,14,64,'ic-warn')}<text class="t-b" x="368" y="104" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">root</text><text class="t" x="368" y="126" text-anchor="middle">master key</text>
<text class="t" x="210" y="160" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">one command, your password, written in the log</text>
</svg><figcaption>root is the all-powerful admin account, and the permission gates do not stop it. sudo ("superuser do") lends you root's power for a single command, after you prove it is really you.</figcaption></figure>
${V.like(`<p>A hotel. Guests have a card for their own room. The manager has a master key for every door. <code>sudo</code> is asking the manager to open one door for you: you show your ID (your password), they open it, and a note goes in the log.</p>`)}
${V.why(`<p>Logging in as root all day is dangerous: one typo can wipe the system, and any program you run has total power. sudo lets you stay an ordinary user and borrow root's power only for the one command that needs it. This idea is called <b>least privilege</b>: hold only the keys the job needs.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'sudo'],' ',[2,'apt update']],['<b>sudo.</b> "Run the next command as root." Asks for your own password, then remembers it for a few minutes.','<b>The command.</b> Anything that changes the system: installing software, editing files in <code>/etc</code>, restarting services.'])}
${V.steps([
 ['<b>whoami</b> prints who Linux thinks you are. Right now: an ordinary user.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 150" role="img" aria-label="whoami prints you"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="138" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ whoami</text><text class="t-term t-a" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">you</text></svg>`],
 ['Updating the list of software packages writes into system folders that belong to root. As plain you, apt is refused.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 150" role="img" aria-label="apt update fails with permission denied"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="138" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ apt update</text><text class="t-term t-bad" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">E: Could not open lock file</text><text class="t-term t-bad" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">   /var/lib/apt/lists/lock</text><text class="t-term t-bad" x="16" y="126" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">   (13: Permission denied)</text></svg>`],
 ['Put <b>sudo</b> in front. It asks for <b>your</b> password (not root\'s), then runs just that one command as root.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 150" role="img" aria-label="sudo apt update asks for your password and works"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="138" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ sudo apt update</text><text class="t-term t-warn" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">[sudo] password for you:</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">Reading package lists... Done</text></svg>`],
 ['Proof: <b>sudo whoami</b> prints <b>root</b>. The very next command, without sudo, is plain you again.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 150" role="img" aria-label="sudo whoami prints root, whoami prints you"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="138" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ sudo whoami</text><text class="t-term t-warn" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">root</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ whoami</text><text class="t-term t-a" x="16" y="126" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">you</text></svg>`]])}
${V.rules(V.ok('sudo apt update','System jobs: installing, updating, editing /etc'),V.no('sudo nano notes.txt','Your own files never need it, and the file may end up owned by root'),
 V.no('sudo chmod -R 777 /','Unlocks the whole computer for everyone. A classic way to break a server'),V.ok('sudo !!','Repeats your last command with sudo in front'))}
${V.hook(`Be yourself by default. Borrow root for one command. Hand the key straight back.`)}
`)}

<div class="try"><b>Try it in your head</b>1. Decode <code>640</code>. <i>rw-r-----: owner reads and writes, group reads, others nothing.</i> 2. bob owns a file set to <code>---r--r--</code>. Can bob read it? <i>No. He matches the owner gate first, and the owner set is empty.</i> 3. Which number for a private SSH key? <i>600.</i></div>
`);

explain('l3',`
<p>One day a website you look after will be slow, or simply gone. The engineers who fix it fast are not guessing: they look at what is running, read what it said, and only then change something. This lesson is that routine.</p>

${V.card(1,'Processes and PIDs','every running program has a number',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 210" role="img" aria-label="Three running programs, each with a PID. PID 3117, node leak.js, uses 99 percent of the CPU"><text class="t-b" x="18" y="22" style="font-size:14px">PID</text><text class="t-b" x="84" y="22" style="font-size:14px">COMMAND</text><text class="t-b" x="252" y="22" style="font-size:14px">CPU</text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="32" width="408" height="44" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="18" y="61" style="font-size:18px;font-weight:700">1</text><text class="t-m" x="84" y="61" style="font-size:16px">systemd</text><rect class="ln-d" x="252" y="44" width="110" height="20" rx="4"/><rect class="bx-ok" x="252" y="44" width="4" height="20" rx="4"/><text class="t-m" x="406" y="60" text-anchor="end" style="font-size:14px">0.1%</text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="84" width="408" height="44" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="18" y="113" style="font-size:18px;font-weight:700">842</text><text class="t-m" x="84" y="113" style="font-size:16px">sshd</text><rect class="ln-d" x="252" y="96" width="110" height="20" rx="4"/><rect class="bx-ok" x="252" y="96" width="4" height="20" rx="4"/><text class="t-m" x="406" y="112" text-anchor="end" style="font-size:14px">0.3%</text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="136" width="408" height="44" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="18" y="165" style="font-size:18px;font-weight:700">3117</text><text class="t-m" x="84" y="165" style="font-size:16px">node leak.js</text><rect class="ln-d" x="252" y="148" width="110" height="20" rx="4"/><rect class="bx-bad" x="252" y="148" width="109" height="20" rx="4"/><text class="t-m" x="406" y="164" text-anchor="end" style="font-size:14px">99.2%</text><text class="t" x="210" y="202" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">every running program gets its own number</text></svg><figcaption>Every running program is a <b>process</b>, and Linux gives each one a <b>PID</b> (process ID). This one is eating almost the whole processor, which is why the fan is screaming.</figcaption></figure>
${V.like(`<p>A busy restaurant kitchen. Every dish being cooked gets an order ticket with a number. If one dish is burning, the chef doesn't shout "stop the pasta!" (there might be three pastas). They shout "cancel ticket 3117!".</p>`)}
${V.why(`<p>A computer runs hundreds of programs at once, often several with the same name. Each one is a <b>process</b>, and the kernel (the core of Linux) gives it a unique <b>PID</b> so you can point at exactly one. <code>top</code> shows them live; <code>ps aux</code> prints a snapshot of all of them.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'kill'],' ',[2,'-9'],' ',[3,'3117']],[
 '<b>kill.</b> Despite the name, it sends a <b>signal</b>: a short message to a process.',
 '<b>Which signal.</b> Leave it out and you send SIGTERM (number 15): "please stop". <code>-9</code> is SIGKILL: "you are stopped now".',
 '<b>PID.</b> Which process. Always a number, never a name.'])}
${V.steps([
 ['<b>top</b> shows live processes, busiest first. PID <b>3117</b>, <b>node leak.js</b>, is using 99% of the CPU. Press q to quit top.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 186" role="img" aria-label="top shows PID 3117 at 99 percent CPU"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="174" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ top</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">  PID USER  %CPU %MEM COMMAND</text><text class="t-term t-bad" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre"> 3117 you   99.2 45.1 node leak.js</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="126" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">  842 root   0.3  0.1 sshd</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="156" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">    1 root   0.1  0.2 systemd</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>kill 3117</b> sends the polite signal <b>SIGTERM</b>: "please finish up and stop". This program ignores it, so it is still there.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 186" role="img" aria-label="kill 3117 sends SIGTERM, the process ignores it"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="174" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ kill 3117</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ ps aux | grep leak</text><text class="t-term t-bad" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">you  3117 99.1 45.1 node leak.js</text><text class="t-term t-warn" x="16" y="126" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre"># still running: it ignored SIGTERM</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>kill -9 3117</b> sends <b>SIGKILL</b>. That one cannot be ignored: the kernel removes the process at once, with no chance to save or clean up.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 186" role="img" aria-label="kill -9 removes the process"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="174" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ kill -9 3117</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ ps aux | grep leak</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre"># nothing: the process is gone</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="126" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre"># CPU back to calm</text></svg>`]])}
${V.rules(V.rh('Rules'),
 V.ok('kill 3117 first','SIGTERM lets the program save its work and close files'),V.ok('kill -9 3117 second','Only when the polite way is ignored'),
 V.no('kill node','kill wants a PID. To stop by name use pkill node, carefully'),V.no('kill -9 1','PID 1 is systemd, the parent of everything. Never'),
 V.rh('Conventions'),V.ok('ps aux | grep node','Find the PID of a program by name'))}
${V.hook(`Find the number, ask nicely (<code>kill</code>), then insist (<code>kill -9</code>).`)}
`)}

${V.card(2,'Services and systemd','programs that run in the background',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 196" role="img" aria-label="systemd at the top looks after three services: nginx has failed, ssh and cron are running"><rect class="bx-a" x="130" y="8" width="160" height="52" rx="8"/>${V.ic('gear',140,14,40,'ic-a')}<text class="t-m" x="186" y="42" style="font-size:18px;font-weight:700">systemd</text><path class="ln" d="M210 60V78H70V96M210 78V96M210 78H350V96"/><rect class="bx-bad" x="10" y="96" width="120" height="52" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="70" y="128.3" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">nginx</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="150" y="96" width="120" height="52" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="210" y="128.3" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">ssh</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="290" y="96" width="120" height="52" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="350" y="128.3" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">cron</text><text class="t-b t-bad" x="70" y="176" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">failed</text><text class="t-b t-ok" x="210" y="176" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">running</text><text class="t-b t-ok" x="350" y="176" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">running</text></svg><figcaption>A <b>service</b> is a program that runs in the background all the time, like a web server. <b>systemd</b> starts them when the machine boots, restarts them when asked, and records what they say.</figcaption></figure>
${V.like(`<p>The caretaker of a big school. Every morning they switch on the heating, the lights and the lifts. If you ask, they restart one. And they keep a diary of everything that happened, called the journal.</p>`)}
${V.why(`<p>A server's important programs (web server, database, SSH) must start by themselves when the machine boots and keep running with nobody logged in. Most Linux systems hand that job to <b>systemd</b>, the very first process (PID 1). You talk to it with <code>systemctl</code>.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'sudo'],' ',[2,'systemctl'],' ',[3,'restart'],' ',[4,'nginx']],[
 '<b>sudo.</b> Changing a service needs root. Just looking (<code>status</code>) doesn\'t.',
 '<b>systemctl.</b> "System control": the remote control for systemd.',
 '<b>Verb.</b> <code>status</code>, <code>start</code>, <code>stop</code>, <code>restart</code>, or <code>enable</code> (start automatically at every boot).',
 '<b>Service name.</b> Officially <code>nginx.service</code>; the ending can be left off.'])}
${V.rules(V.ok('systemctl status nginx','Is it running? Since when? Last few log lines'),V.ok('sudo systemctl enable nginx','Start it at every boot. start alone only starts it now'),
 V.no('sudo reboot','Turning the whole server off and on hides the cause and takes everything down'))}
${V.hook(`systemd is the caretaker; <code>systemctl</code> is how you talk to it.`)}
`)}

${V.card(3,'Logs: the program tells you what is wrong','look, read, fix, test, restart',`
${V.like(`<p>A car's dashboard. When a warning light comes on, a good mechanic reads the code before opening the bonnet. Logs are the program's warning lights, and they nearly always say exactly what is wrong and where.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'journalctl'],' ',[2,'-u nginx'],' ',[3,'-n 50']],[
 '<b>journalctl.</b> Reads systemd\'s journal: everything services have printed.',
 '<b>-u (unit).</b> Only show lines from this one service.',
 '<b>-n 50 (optional).</b> Only the last 50 lines. <code>-f</code> instead keeps following new lines as they arrive.'])}
<p><b>Watch an on-call engineer fix nginx</b>, one careful step at a time.</p>
${V.steps([
 ['Step one is always <b>look</b>. <b>systemctl status</b> says nginx is not running: it <b>failed</b> when it tried to start.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 156" role="img" aria-label="systemctl status shows nginx failed"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="144" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ systemctl status nginx</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre"> nginx.service - A high performance</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">   web server</text><text class="t-term t-bad" x="16" y="126" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">   Active: failed (Result: exit-code)</text></svg>`],
 ['Next, <b>read the logs</b>. <b>journalctl -u nginx</b> shows what nginx said before it died. The line ends with the file and the line number: <b>default:2</b>.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 156" role="img" aria-label="journalctl shows the error points at default line 2"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="144" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ journalctl -u nginx</text><text class="t-term t-bad" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">nginx: [emerg] invalid number of</text><text class="t-term t-bad" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">  arguments in "listen" directive</text><text class="t-term t-warn" x="16" y="126" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">  in /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/default:2</text></svg>`],
 ['Open that file and look at line 2. Every nginx setting must end with a semicolon, and this one does not.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 186" role="img" aria-label="Line 2 of the config is missing a semicolon"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="174" rx="8"/><text class="t-term t-a" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre"># /etc/nginx/sites-available/default</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">server {</text><text class="t-term t-bad" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">    listen 80      &#8592; line 2</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="126" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">    root /var/www/html;</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="156" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">}</text></svg>`],
 ['Add the <b>;</b>, then <b>test</b> before restarting. <b>nginx -t</b> checks the config without touching the running server.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 186" role="img" aria-label="nginx -t says the config is ok"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="174" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ sudo nginx -t</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">nginx: the configuration file</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">  /etc/nginx/nginx.conf syntax is ok</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="126" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">nginx: configuration file</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="156" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">  /etc/nginx/nginx.conf test is successful</text></svg>`],
 ['Only now <b>restart</b>, and check the result. The site answers again.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 156" role="img" aria-label="restart nginx and curl shows It works"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="144" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ sudo systemctl restart nginx</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ curl localhost</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">&lt;h1&gt;It works!&lt;/h1&gt;</text></svg>`]])}
${V.rules(V.rh('Rules'),
 V.ok('read the log first','The log names the file and the line. Restarting without reading only hides the problem'),
 V.ok('sudo nginx -t','Test the config before every restart'),V.no('restart and hope','A broken config means the restart fails too, and now the site is fully down'),
 V.rh('Conventions'),V.ok('journalctl -u nginx -f','Watch the log live while you test in another window'))}
${V.build(`<ol><li>Find the busy process with <code>top</code> and note its PID.</li><li>Stop it politely, check, then force it if it ignores you.</li><li>Ask systemd for the status of the web server.</li><li>Read its journal and find the file name and line number.</li><li>Fix that line, test the config, restart, and confirm with <code>curl localhost</code>.</li></ol>`)}
${V.hook(`Look, read, fix, test, restart. In that order, every time.`)}
`)}

<div class="try"><b>Try it in your head</b>1. Which signal does plain <code>kill</code> send? <i>SIGTERM, the polite one.</i> 2. A service must survive a reboot. Which verb? <i>enable.</i> 3. nginx won't start. What do you run before changing anything? <i>systemctl status nginx and journalctl -u nginx.</i></div>
`);

explain('l4',`
<p>"Which visitor is hammering our server?" "How many errors since breakfast?" On a real server, engineers answer questions like these in seconds, by snapping together tiny tools into one line.</p>

${V.card(1,'The pipe','snap small tools together',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 170" role="img" aria-label="grep keeps the ERROR lines from app.log, the pipe carries them into wc -l, which counts them: 3"><rect class="bx-info" x="6" y="30" width="70" height="90" rx="8"/>${V.ic('file',17,42,48,'ic-info')}<text class="t-m" x="41" y="140" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">app.log</text><path class="ln" d="M76 75H92"/><polygon class="ah" points="90,68 90,82 100,75"/><rect class="bx-a" x="100" y="30" width="110" height="90" rx="8"/>${V.ic('search',131,38,48,'ic-a')}<text class="t-m" x="155" y="108" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px;font-weight:700">grep</text><rect class="bx-warn" x="210" y="62" width="60" height="26" rx="4"/><text class="t-m" x="240" y="81" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:20px;font-weight:700">|</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="270" y="30" width="100" height="90" rx="8"/>${V.ic('list',296,38,48,'ic-ok')}<text class="t-m" x="320" y="108" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px;font-weight:700">wc -l</text><path class="ln-ok" d="M370 75H384"/><polygon class="ah-ok" points="382,68 382,82 392,75"/><text class="t-m" x="406" y="82" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:24px;font-weight:700">3</text><text class="t-b" x="240" y="140" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">the pipe</text><text class="t" x="155" y="162" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">keep ERROR lines</text><text class="t" x="320" y="162" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">count lines</text></svg><figcaption>Two small tools joined by a pipe <code>|</code>. grep's output never reaches the screen: it flows straight into wc, and only the final answer is printed.</figcaption></figure>
${V.like(`<p>A factory conveyor belt. Each machine does one simple job (cut, paint, count) and drops its work on the belt for the next machine. The pipe <code>|</code> is the belt.</p>`)}
${V.why(`<p>In the early 1970s, Doug McIlroy at Bell Labs pushed for programs to be joined "like garden hoses". Unix added the pipe in 1973, and with it a rule that still holds: write small tools that each do one thing well, and connect them.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,"awk '{print $1}' access.log"],' ',[2,'|'],' ',[3,'sort'],' ',[2,'|'],' ',[4,'uniq -c'],' ',[2,'|'],' ',[5,'sort -rn'],' ',[2,'|'],' ',[6,'head -3']],[
 '<b>Pick a column.</b> Print the first word of every line: the IP address.',
 '<b>Pipe.</b> Output of the left side becomes input of the right side.',
 '<b>Group.</b> Sort so identical lines sit together.',
 '<b>Count.</b> Merge each run of identical lines and put the count in front.',
 '<b>Rank.</b> Numeric (<code>-n</code>), reversed (<code>-r</code>): biggest first.',
 '<b>Trim.</b> Keep the first 3 lines.'])}
<p><b>Watch the data flow</b> through each machine. The highlighted part is the tool that just ran.</p>
${V.steps([
 ['The raw log: one line per visit to the website. The IP address (the visitor\'s number on the internet) is the first word of each line. Question: who visits most?',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 254" role="img" aria-label="Seven raw log lines"><text class="t-m" x="10" y="26" style="font-size:15px">access.log (a few lines)</text><text class="t-m t-dim" x="10" y="50" style="font-size:15px">nothing has run yet</text><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="62" width="412" height="188" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="86" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">203.0.113.9 - - [..] "GET /" 200</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="110" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">198.51.100.4 - - [..] "GET /" 200</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="134" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">10.0.0.7 - - [..] "GET /" 200</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="158" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">203.0.113.9 - - [..] "GET /" 200</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="182" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">192.0.2.33 - - [..] "GET /" 200</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="206" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">198.51.100.4 - - [..] "GET /" 200</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="230" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">203.0.113.9 - - [..] "GET /" 200</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>awk \'{print $1}\'</b> keeps only the first column. Seven lines in, seven IP addresses out.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 254" role="img" aria-label="awk prints only the IPs"><text class="t-m" x="10" y="26" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre"><tspan class="t-a" style="font-weight:700">awk '{print $1}' access.log</tspan><tspan class="t-dim"> | sort</tspan></text><text class="t-m" x="10" y="50" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre"><tspan class="t-dim"> | uniq -c</tspan><tspan class="t-dim"> | sort -rn</tspan><tspan class="t-dim"> | head -3</tspan></text><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="62" width="412" height="188" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="86" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">203.0.113.9</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="110" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">198.51.100.4</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="134" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">10.0.0.7</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="158" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">203.0.113.9</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="182" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">192.0.2.33</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="206" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">198.51.100.4</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="230" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">203.0.113.9</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>sort</b> puts identical lines next to each other, like sorting cards into piles.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 254" role="img" aria-label="sort groups identical IPs together"><text class="t-m" x="10" y="26" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre"><tspan>awk '{print $1}' access.log</tspan><tspan class="t-a" style="font-weight:700"> | sort</tspan></text><text class="t-m" x="10" y="50" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre"><tspan class="t-dim"> | uniq -c</tspan><tspan class="t-dim"> | sort -rn</tspan><tspan class="t-dim"> | head -3</tspan></text><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="62" width="412" height="188" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="86" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">10.0.0.7</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="110" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">192.0.2.33</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="134" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">198.51.100.4</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="158" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">198.51.100.4</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="182" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">203.0.113.9</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="206" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">203.0.113.9</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="230" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">203.0.113.9</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>uniq -c</b> squashes each pile into one line and writes how many there were in front. It only merges <b>neighbours</b>, which is why sort had to come first.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 254" role="img" aria-label="uniq -c counts each IP"><text class="t-m" x="10" y="26" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre"><tspan>awk '{print $1}' access.log</tspan><tspan> | sort</tspan></text><text class="t-m" x="10" y="50" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre"><tspan class="t-a" style="font-weight:700"> | uniq -c</tspan><tspan class="t-dim"> | sort -rn</tspan><tspan class="t-dim"> | head -3</tspan></text><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="62" width="412" height="116" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="86" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">1 10.0.0.7</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="110" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">1 192.0.2.33</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="134" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">2 198.51.100.4</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="158" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">3 203.0.113.9</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>sort -rn</b> sorts again: <b>n</b> for numeric (so 10 comes after 9), <b>r</b> for reverse, biggest first.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 254" role="img" aria-label="sort -rn puts the biggest count first"><text class="t-m" x="10" y="26" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre"><tspan>awk '{print $1}' access.log</tspan><tspan> | sort</tspan></text><text class="t-m" x="10" y="50" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre"><tspan> | uniq -c</tspan><tspan class="t-a" style="font-weight:700"> | sort -rn</tspan><tspan class="t-dim"> | head -3</tspan></text><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="62" width="412" height="116" rx="8"/><text class="t-term t-a" x="16" y="86" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">3 203.0.113.9</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="110" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">2 198.51.100.4</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="134" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">1 192.0.2.33</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="158" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">1 10.0.0.7</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>head -3</b> keeps only the first three lines. Answer: the busiest visitor made 3 visits. Five tiny tools, one question answered.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 254" role="img" aria-label="head -3 keeps the top three"><text class="t-m" x="10" y="26" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre"><tspan>awk '{print $1}' access.log</tspan><tspan> | sort</tspan></text><text class="t-m" x="10" y="50" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre"><tspan> | uniq -c</tspan><tspan> | sort -rn</tspan><tspan class="t-a" style="font-weight:700"> | head -3</tspan></text><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="62" width="412" height="92" rx="8"/><text class="t-term t-a" x="16" y="86" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">3 203.0.113.9</text><text class="t-term t-a" x="16" y="110" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">2 198.51.100.4</text><text class="t-term t-a" x="16" y="134" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">1 192.0.2.33</text></svg>`]])}
${V.rules(V.rh('Rules'),
 V.ok('a | b','Sends a\'s output into b'),V.no('a &gt; b','Writes a\'s output into a FILE called b, replacing it'),
 V.no('uniq -c without sort','uniq only merges neighbours, so the counts come out wrong'),V.no('sort -r on counts','Without -n, "10" sorts before "9" like words. Use -rn'))}
${V.hook(`One tool, one job. The pipe is the conveyor belt between them.`)}
`)}

${V.card(2,'grep and wc','find the lines, count the lines',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 196" role="img" aria-label="Five log lines go into grep ERROR, only the two ERROR lines come out"><rect class="bx" x="6" y="8" width="120" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="66" y="28.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">INFO</text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="44" width="120" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="66" y="64.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">WARN</text><rect class="bx-bad" x="6" y="80" width="120" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="66" y="100.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">ERROR</text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="116" width="120" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="66" y="136.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">INFO</text><rect class="bx-bad" x="6" y="152" width="120" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="66" y="172.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">ERROR</text><path class="ln" d="M130 96H160"/><polygon class="ah" points="158,89 158,103 168,96"/><rect class="bx-a" x="168" y="52" width="96" height="90" rx="8"/>${V.ic('search',192,58,48,'ic-a')}<text class="t-m" x="216" y="130" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px;font-weight:700">grep</text><path class="ln-ok" d="M264 96H288"/><polygon class="ah-ok" points="286,89 286,103 296,96"/><rect class="bx-bad" x="296" y="62" width="120" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="356" y="82.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">ERROR</text><rect class="bx-bad" x="296" y="100" width="120" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="356" y="120.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">ERROR</text><text class="t" x="356" y="170" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">only matches</text></svg><figcaption>grep reads every line and lets through only the lines that contain your pattern. Everything else is dropped.</figcaption></figure>
${V.like(`<p>A sieve. Pour every line of the file in; only the lines containing your word stay in the sieve.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'grep'],' ',[2,'-c'],' ',[3,"' 500 '"],' ',[4,'access.log']],[
 '<b>grep.</b> Search for a pattern, line by line.',
 '<b>-c (count).</b> Print how many lines matched instead of the lines. Others: <code>-i</code> ignore case, <code>-v</code> keep the lines that do NOT match, <code>-n</code> show line numbers, <code>-r</code> search a whole folder.',
 '<b>Pattern.</b> In quotes because of the spaces. The spaces make sure you match the status 500, not a size like 1500.',
 '<b>File.</b> Leave it out and grep reads from a pipe instead.'])}
${V.rules(V.ok("grep 'Payment provider' app.log",'Quote patterns that contain spaces'),V.no('grep error app.log','grep is case-sensitive: this misses ERROR. Use -i'),
 V.ok('wc -l access.log','Counts lines. Also works at the end of a pipe: grep ERROR app.log | wc -l'))}
${V.hook(`grep finds, <code>-c</code> counts, <code>-v</code> flips, <code>-i</code> ignores case.`)}
`)}

${V.card(3,'awk and sed','cut columns, swap words',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 184" role="img" aria-label="awk splits a log line at every space: $1 is the IP, $6 is GET, $9 is the status 200"><rect class="bx-ok" x="4" y="8" width="116" height="36" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="62" y="30.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">203.0.113.9</text><text class="t-b t-a" x="62.0" y="62" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">$1</text><rect class="bx" x="124" y="8" width="30" height="36" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="139" y="30.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">-</text><text class="t-b t-a" x="139.0" y="62" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">$2</text><rect class="bx" x="158" y="8" width="30" height="36" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="173" y="30.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">-</text><text class="t-b t-a" x="173.0" y="62" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">$3</text><rect class="bx" x="192" y="8" width="224" height="36" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="304" y="30.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">[09/Oct/2026:10:10:02</text><text class="t-b t-a" x="304.0" y="62" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">$4</text><rect class="bx" x="4" y="96" width="70" height="36" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="39" y="118.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">+0000]</text><text class="t-b t-a" x="39.0" y="150" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">$5</text><rect class="bx" x="78" y="96" width="56" height="36" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="106" y="118.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">"GET</text><text class="t-b t-a" x="106.0" y="150" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">$6</text><rect class="bx" x="138" y="96" width="30" height="36" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="153" y="118.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">/</text><text class="t-b t-a" x="153.0" y="150" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">$7</text><rect class="bx" x="172" y="96" width="96" height="36" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="220" y="118.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">HTTP/1.1"</text><text class="t-b t-a" x="220.0" y="150" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">$8</text><rect class="bx-warn" x="272" y="96" width="56" height="36" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="300" y="118.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">200</text><text class="t-b t-a" x="300.0" y="150" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">$9</text><rect class="bx" x="332" y="96" width="84" height="36" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="374" y="118.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">512</text><text class="t-b t-a" x="374.0" y="150" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">$10</text></svg><figcaption>awk cuts each line wherever there is a space and numbers the pieces. In this log, <code>$1</code> is the visitor's IP and <code>$9</code> is the status code.</figcaption></figure>
${V.like(`<p>awk is a pair of scissors that cuts every line into numbered strips. sed is "find and replace" from a word processor, but it works on files you never open.</p>`)}
${V.why(`<p>Both were born at Bell Labs in the 1970s (awk is named after its three creators: Aho, Weinberger and Kernighan). They are still on every Linux server today, which is why they beat any fancy tool when you are logged into a machine you don't control.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'sed'],' ',[2,'-i'],' ',[3,"'s/"],[4,'DEBUG=true'],[3,'/'],[5,'DEBUG=false'],[3,"/'"],' ',[6,'.env']],[
 '<b>sed.</b> The "stream editor".',
 '<b>-i (in place).</b> Change the file itself. Without it, sed only prints the result.',
 '<b>s/ / /.</b> The substitute command and its separators. Add <code>g</code> at the end (<code>/g</code>) to replace every match on a line, not just the first.',
 '<b>Find.</b> The text to look for.',
 '<b>Replace.</b> What to put instead.',
 '<b>File.</b>'])}
${V.steps([
 ['The file <b>.env</b> holds settings. DEBUG is switched on, which a live server should never have.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 156" role="img" aria-label=".env with DEBUG=true"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="144" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ cat .env</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">PORT=3000</text><text class="t-term t-bad" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">DEBUG=true</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="126" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">LOG_LEVEL=info</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>Without -i</b>, sed prints the changed text to the screen but leaves the file alone. Handy as a safe preview.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 156" role="img" aria-label="sed without -i only prints"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="144" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ sed 's/DEBUG=true/DEBUG=false/' .env</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">... DEBUG=false   (on screen only)</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ cat .env</text><text class="t-term t-bad" x="16" y="126" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">... DEBUG=true    (file unchanged)</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>With -i</b> (in place), sed rewrites the file itself. Check with cat: the setting is now off.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 186" role="img" aria-label="sed -i changes the file"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="174" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ sed -i 's/DEBUG=true/DEBUG=false/' .env</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ cat .env</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">PORT=3000</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="126" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">DEBUG=false</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="156" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">LOG_LEVEL=info</text></svg>`]])}
${V.rules(V.rh('Rules'),
 V.ok("awk '{print $1}'","Single quotes, so the shell doesn't swap $1 for something else"),V.no('awk "{print $1}"','In double quotes the shell replaces $1 before awk sees it'),
 V.no('sed -i without a preview','There is no undo. Run it once without -i first'),
 V.rh('Conventions'),V.ok("sed -i '' 's/a/b/' f",'On a Mac (BSD sed), -i needs an extra empty argument'))}
${V.build(`<ol><li>Show only the error lines from the app log with grep.</li><li>Count how many requests got a 500, using grep's count flag and a pattern with spaces.</li><li>Rank the top 3 visitors: awk, sort, uniq -c, sort -rn, head.</li><li>Preview the DEBUG change with sed, then run it again with <code>-i</code> and check with <code>cat</code>.</li><li>Count all the lines in the access log with <code>wc -l</code>.</li></ol>`)}
${V.hook(`awk cuts columns, sed swaps words, and <code>-i</code> means "for real".`)}
`)}

<div class="try"><b>Try it in your head</b>1. What does <code>grep -v INFO app.log</code> show? <i>Every line that does NOT contain INFO.</i> 2. Why sort before uniq -c? <i>uniq only merges lines that sit next to each other.</i> 3. In the access log, which awk field is the status code? <i>$9.</i></div>
`);

explain('l5',`
<p>If you type the same five commands every day, you are doing a robot's job. A Bash script writes them down once; cron, the server's alarm clock, runs them for you while you sleep. This is how backups, reports and clean-ups happen on real servers.</p>

${V.card(1,'A script is a saved recipe','commands in a file',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" role="img" aria-label="backup.sh is a text file of commands. The first line, #!/bin/bash, tells Linux to run it with bash"><rect class="bx" x="6" y="6" width="260" height="188" rx="8"/>${V.ic('file',222,12,36,'ic-info')}<text class="t-m t-a" x="18" y="34" style="font-size:16px;font-weight:700">#!/bin/bash</text><text class="t-m" x="18" y="62" style="font-size:15px">set -e</text><text class="t-m" x="18" y="90" style="font-size:15px">mkdir -p "$DEST"</text><text class="t-m" x="18" y="118" style="font-size:15px">cp a.txt "$DEST/"</text><text class="t-m" x="18" y="146" style="font-size:15px">echo "Done"</text><text class="t-b" x="18" y="178" style="font-size:15px">backup.sh</text><path class="ln-a" d="M294 29H144"/><polygon class="ah-a" points="146,22 146,36 136,29"/><text class="t t-a" x="300" y="24" style="font-size:14px">which program</text><text class="t t-a" x="300" y="42" style="font-size:14px">runs this file</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="290" y="92" width="124" height="44" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="352" y="119.6" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px;font-weight:700">chmod +x</text><text class="t" x="352" y="162" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">then run:</text><text class="t-m" x="352" y="184" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">./backup.sh</text></svg><figcaption>A script is just the commands you would type, saved in a file. The first line, the <b>shebang</b>, names the program that should read it. Make it executable once, then run it like any command.</figcaption></figure>
${V.like(`<p>A recipe card. Instead of remembering every step each time, you write them down in order, and anyone (including a machine at 2 a.m.) can follow the card exactly.</p>`)}
${V.why(`<p>The shell you type into, <b>Bash</b> (1989), is also a small programming language. Saving commands in a file makes a job repeatable, shareable and impossible to half-forget.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'#!'],[2,'/bin/bash']],[
 '<b>Shebang.</b> Hash and exclamation mark. Must be the very first two characters of the file.',
 '<b>Interpreter.</b> The full path of the program that will read the rest. Here, Bash.'])}
<p><b>Watch the script run</b>, one line at a time. The arrow shows the line being run.</p>
${V.steps([
 ['<b>set -e</b> switches on a safety rule: if any command fails, stop the whole script there.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 236" role="img" aria-label="set -e"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="44" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="34" style="font-size:16px;white-space:pre"><tspan class="t-a">&#9654; </tspan>set -e</text><text class="t-m" x="8" y="78" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">DEST</text><rect class="bx" x="60" y="58" width="240" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m t-dim" x="180" y="79.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">(empty)</text><rect class="bx" x="4" y="102" width="412" height="58" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="14" y="124" style="font-size:14px">~/docs</text><text class="t-m" x="14" y="148" style="font-size:14px">a.txt</text><text class="t-m" x="73.0" y="148" style="font-size:14px">b.txt</text><text class="t-m" x="132.0" y="148" style="font-size:14px">c.txt</text></svg>`],
 ['The part inside <b>$( )</b> runs first: <b>date +%F</b> prints today\'s date. The result is glued into the text and stored in the variable <b>DEST</b>.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 236" role="img" aria-label="DEST is set to backup-2026-10-09"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="44" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="34" style="font-size:16px;white-space:pre"><tspan class="t-a">&#9654; </tspan>DEST="backup-$(date +%F)"</text><text class="t-m" x="8" y="78" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">DEST</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="60" y="58" width="240" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="180" y="79.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">backup-2026-10-09</text><text class="t t-a" x="312" y="80" style="font-size:14px">date +%F</text><rect class="bx" x="4" y="102" width="412" height="58" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="14" y="124" style="font-size:14px">~/docs</text><text class="t-m" x="14" y="148" style="font-size:14px">a.txt</text><text class="t-m" x="73.0" y="148" style="font-size:14px">b.txt</text><text class="t-m" x="132.0" y="148" style="font-size:14px">c.txt</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>[ -d "$DEST" ]</b> asks "is there a directory with this name?". Not yet, so the lines between <b>then</b> and <b>fi</b> are skipped.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 236" role="img" aria-label="the if test is false"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="44" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="34" style="font-size:16px;white-space:pre"><tspan class="t-a">&#9654; </tspan>if [ -d "$DEST" ]; then</text><text class="t-m" x="8" y="78" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">DEST</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="60" y="58" width="240" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="180" y="79.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">backup-2026-10-09</text><rect class="bx" x="4" y="102" width="412" height="58" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="14" y="124" style="font-size:14px">~/docs</text><text class="t-m" x="14" y="148" style="font-size:14px">a.txt</text><text class="t-m" x="73.0" y="148" style="font-size:14px">b.txt</text><text class="t-m" x="132.0" y="148" style="font-size:14px">c.txt</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="10" y="186" style="font-size:15px">test: false, skip to fi</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>mkdir -p "$DEST"</b> creates the dated folder. "$DEST" is replaced by the value in the box.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 236" role="img" aria-label="the backup folder is created"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="44" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="34" style="font-size:16px;white-space:pre"><tspan class="t-a">&#9654; </tspan>mkdir -p "$DEST"</text><text class="t-m" x="8" y="78" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">DEST</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="60" y="58" width="240" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="180" y="79.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">backup-2026-10-09</text><rect class="bx" x="4" y="102" width="412" height="58" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="14" y="124" style="font-size:14px">~/docs</text><text class="t-m" x="14" y="148" style="font-size:14px">a.txt</text><text class="t-m" x="73.0" y="148" style="font-size:14px">b.txt</text><text class="t-m" x="132.0" y="148" style="font-size:14px">c.txt</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="200" y="110" width="210" height="44" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="210" y="128" style="font-size:14px">backup-2026-10-09/</text><text class="t-m t-dim" x="210" y="148" style="font-size:14px">(empty)</text></svg>`],
 ['The <b>for</b> loop runs its body once for each file matching <b>*.txt</b>, with <b>f</b> holding a different name each time.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 236" role="img" aria-label="the loop copies three files"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="44" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="34" style="font-size:16px;white-space:pre"><tspan class="t-a">&#9654; </tspan>for f in *.txt; do cp "$f" ...</text><text class="t-m" x="8" y="78" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">DEST</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="60" y="58" width="240" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="180" y="79.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">backup-2026-10-09</text><rect class="bx" x="4" y="102" width="412" height="58" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="14" y="124" style="font-size:14px">~/docs</text><text class="t-m" x="14" y="148" style="font-size:14px">a.txt</text><text class="t-m" x="73.0" y="148" style="font-size:14px">b.txt</text><text class="t-m" x="132.0" y="148" style="font-size:14px">c.txt</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="200" y="110" width="210" height="44" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="210" y="128" style="font-size:14px">backup-2026-10-09/</text><text class="t-m" x="210" y="148" style="font-size:14px">a.txt b.txt c.txt</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="10" y="186" style="font-size:15px">Backed up a.txt</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="10" y="208" style="font-size:15px">Backed up b.txt</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="10" y="230" style="font-size:15px">Backed up c.txt</text></svg>`],
 ['Run it again the same day. Now the test is <b>true</b>, so the script prints its message and <b>exit 0</b> ends it early. Nothing is copied twice.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 236" role="img" aria-label="second run stops early"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="44" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="34" style="font-size:16px;white-space:pre"><tspan class="t-a">&#9654; </tspan>if [ -d "$DEST" ]; then</text><text class="t-m" x="8" y="78" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">DEST</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="60" y="58" width="240" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="180" y="79.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">backup-2026-10-09</text><rect class="bx" x="4" y="102" width="412" height="58" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="14" y="124" style="font-size:14px">~/docs</text><text class="t-m" x="14" y="148" style="font-size:14px">a.txt</text><text class="t-m" x="73.0" y="148" style="font-size:14px">b.txt</text><text class="t-m" x="132.0" y="148" style="font-size:14px">c.txt</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="200" y="110" width="210" height="44" rx="6"/><text class="t-m" x="210" y="128" style="font-size:14px">backup-2026-10-09/</text><text class="t-m" x="210" y="148" style="font-size:14px">a.txt b.txt c.txt</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="10" y="186" style="font-size:15px">Already backed up today</text></svg>`]])}
${V.rules(V.rh('Rules'),
 V.ok('#!/bin/bash on line 1','Nothing before it, not even a blank line'),V.ok('chmod +x backup.sh','Without x, ./backup.sh gives Permission denied'),
 V.ok('set -e','Stop at the first failure, so a broken step can\'t lead to a worse one'))}
${V.hook(`Shebang, set -e, chmod +x, then <code>./</code> to run.`)}
`)}

${V.card(2,'Variables, if and for','the grammar of a script',`
${V.anat([[1,'if'],' ',[2,'['],' ',[3,'-d'],' ',[4,'"$DEST"'],' ',[2,']'],[5,'; then'],'\n  echo "Already backed up today"\n',[6,'fi']],[
 '<b>if.</b> Run the next block only when the test passes.',
 '<b>[ ]</b> The test. The brackets need a space on both sides, because <code>[</code> is really a command.',
 '<b>-d.</b> "Is it a directory?" Others: <code>-f</code> is it a file, <code>-z</code> is the text empty.',
 '<b>"$DEST".</b> <code>$</code> reads the variable. The quotes keep a name with spaces in one piece.',
 '<b>; then.</b> End of the test, start of the block.',
 '<b>fi.</b> "if" backwards: end of the block. A loop ends with <code>done</code>.'])}
${V.like(`<p>A variable is a labelled jar. <code>DEST="backup"</code> puts something in the jar; <code>$DEST</code> means "open the jar and use what is inside".</p>`)}
${V.rules(V.rh('Rules: Bash is picky about spaces'),
 V.ok('DEST="backup"','No spaces around ='),V.no('DEST = "backup"','With spaces, Bash tries to run a command called DEST'),
 V.no('[-d "$DEST"]','No spaces inside the brackets: command not found'),V.no('cp $f "$DEST/"','Unquoted: a file called "my notes.txt" becomes two names'),
 V.rh('Conventions'),V.ok('"$f" every time','Always quote variables'),V.ok('DEST, BACKUP_DIR','Capitals for script settings, lower case for loop variables'))}
${V.hook(`No spaces round <code>=</code>, spaces inside <code>[ ]</code>, quotes round every <code>"$var"</code>.`)}
`)}

${V.card(3,'cron','the server\'s alarm clock',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 176" role="img" aria-label="A cron line has five time fields: minute 0, hour 2, then three stars for any day, any month, any weekday"><rect class="bx-a" x="4" y="10" width="76" height="58" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="42" y="48.1" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:26px;font-weight:700">0</text><text class="t-b" x="42" y="92" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">minute</text><rect class="bx-a" x="86" y="10" width="76" height="58" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="124" y="48.1" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:26px;font-weight:700">2</text><text class="t-b" x="124" y="92" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">hour</text><rect class="bx" x="168" y="10" width="76" height="58" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="206" y="48.1" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:26px;font-weight:700">*</text><text class="t-b" x="206" y="92" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">day</text><rect class="bx" x="250" y="10" width="76" height="58" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="288" y="48.1" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:26px;font-weight:700">*</text><text class="t-b" x="288" y="92" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">month</text><rect class="bx" x="332" y="10" width="76" height="58" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="370" y="48.1" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:26px;font-weight:700">*</text><text class="t-b" x="370" y="92" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">weekday</text><text class="t-m" x="210" y="128" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">runs: /home/you/docs/backup.sh</text><text class="t-b t-a" x="210" y="160" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px">"at 02:00, every day"</text></svg><figcaption>A cron line is an alarm clock with five dials. A number means "exactly this"; a star means "any". This one rings at minute 0 of hour 2, on any day, in any month, on any weekday.</figcaption></figure>
${V.why(`<p>cron has been part of Unix since the 1970s. Its name comes from Chronos, the Greek word for time. Each user has a list of jobs called a <b>crontab</b> (cron table): edit it with <code>crontab -e</code>, show it with <code>crontab -l</code>.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'0'],' ',[2,'2'],' ',[3,'*'],' ',[4,'*'],' ',[5,'*'],' ',[6,'/home/you/docs/backup.sh']],[
 '<b>Minute</b> (0 to 59).','<b>Hour</b> (0 to 23, 24-hour clock).','<b>Day of the month</b> (1 to 31).','<b>Month</b> (1 to 12).','<b>Day of the week</b> (0 to 7, where 0 and 7 are both Sunday).',
 '<b>Command.</b> Use the full path: cron does not start in your folder.'])}
${V.steps([
 ['Every minute, cron wakes up and compares the clock with each line. 01:59: hour is 1, not 2. No match.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 170" role="img" aria-label="01:59 no match"><rect class="bx" x="6" y="10" width="140" height="64" rx="8"/>${V.ic('clock',14,20,44,'ic-info')}<text class="t-m" x="110" y="52" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700">01:59</text><text class="t-m" x="164" y="34" style="font-size:20px;font-weight:700">0 2 * * *</text><text class="t t-bad" x="164" y="62" style="font-size:15px">hour 1 is not 2</text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="96" width="408" height="60" rx="8"/><text class="t t-dim" x="210" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">nothing runs</text></svg>`],
 ['02:00: minute 0 matches, hour 2 matches, and the stars match any day. Cron runs the script.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 170" role="img" aria-label="02:00 matches, script runs"><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="10" width="140" height="64" rx="8"/>${V.ic('clock',14,20,44,'ic-ok')}<text class="t-m" x="110" y="52" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700">02:00</text><text class="t-m" x="164" y="34" style="font-size:20px;font-weight:700">0 2 * * *</text><text class="t t-ok" x="164" y="62" style="font-size:15px">all five fields match</text><rect class="bx-dark" x="6" y="96" width="408" height="60" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="18" y="122" style="font-size:15px">$ /home/you/docs/backup.sh</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="18" y="146" style="font-size:15px">Backed up a.txt ...</text></svg>`],
 ['02:01: minute 1 is not 0. No match until 02:00 tomorrow.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 170" role="img" aria-label="02:01 no match"><rect class="bx" x="6" y="10" width="140" height="64" rx="8"/>${V.ic('clock',14,20,44,'ic-info')}<text class="t-m" x="110" y="52" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700">02:01</text><text class="t-m" x="164" y="34" style="font-size:20px;font-weight:700">0 2 * * *</text><text class="t t-bad" x="164" y="62" style="font-size:15px">minute 1 is not 0</text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="96" width="408" height="60" rx="8"/><text class="t t-dim" x="210" y="132" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">nothing runs</text></svg>`]])}
${V.rules(V.ok('*/15 * * * *','Every 15 minutes: */n means "every n"'),V.ok('0 9 * * 1','09:00 every Monday'),
 V.no('0 2 * * * backup.sh','Relative path: cron won\'t find it. Use /home/you/docs/backup.sh'),V.no('2 0 * * *','Minute comes first: this is 00:02, not 02:00'))}
${V.build(`<ol><li>Open <code>backup.sh</code> in nano and start with the shebang and <code>set -e</code>.</li><li>Store a dated folder name in a variable with <code>$(date +%F)</code>.</li><li>If that folder already exists, print a message and <code>exit 0</code>.</li><li>Otherwise make it and loop over <code>*.txt</code>, copying each one.</li><li><code>chmod +x</code>, run it twice, then add a 02:00 line with <code>crontab -e</code> and check with <code>crontab -l</code>.</li></ol>`)}
${V.hook(`Minute, hour, day, month, weekday: "My Hungry Dog Munches Wednesdays".`)}
`)}

<div class="try"><b>Try it in your head</b>1. What is wrong with <code>NAME = "ada"</code>? <i>Spaces around =.</i> 2. When does <code>30 18 * * 5</code> run? <i>18:30 every Friday.</i> 3. Why <code>"$f"</code> rather than <code>$f</code>? <i>So file names with spaces stay one name.</i></div>
`);

explain('l6',`
<p>Nearly every server you ever deploy to will be thousands of miles away. SSH is the secure cable you plug into it, and keys are how professionals log in: faster than passwords, and practically impossible to guess.</p>

${V.card(1,'Key pairs','a padlock you hand out, a key you keep',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 212" role="img" aria-label="Your laptop keeps the private key. Copies of the public key, drawn as open padlocks, go to a server and to GitHub"><rect class="bx-a" x="6" y="10" width="150" height="150" rx="8"/>${V.ic('laptop',36,18,90,'ic-a')}${V.ic('key',56,96,48,'ic-warn')}<text class="t-m" x="81" y="184" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">id_ed25519</text><text class="t t-bad" x="81" y="204" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">private: never share</text><path class="ln-d" d="M156 60H262M156 126H262"/><rect class="bx-ok" x="262" y="10" width="152" height="62" rx="8"/>${V.ic('server',270,16,48,'ic-ok')}${V.ic('unlock',356,18,44,'ic-ok')}<text class="t" x="338" y="92" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">web1 server</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="262" y="100" width="152" height="62" rx="8"/>${V.ic('globe',270,106,48,'ic-ok')}${V.ic('unlock',356,108,44,'ic-ok')}<text class="t" x="338" y="182" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">GitHub</text><text class="t t-ok" x="338" y="204" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">id_ed25519.pub: share</text></svg><figcaption>ssh-keygen makes a matching pair. The <b>public</b> key (.pub) is like an open padlock: hand out copies to every server. The <b>private</b> key is the only key that opens them, and it never leaves your laptop.</figcaption></figure>
${V.like(`<p>Imagine a box of identical open padlocks that only your one key can open. You give a padlock to every server ("lock my door with this"). Anyone can see a padlock; it's useless without your key.</p>`)}
${V.why(`<p>Passwords can be guessed, and servers on the internet get thousands of guessing attempts a day. A key pair is two linked numbers made with maths that is easy one way and practically impossible to reverse. <b>Ed25519</b> is the modern, recommended kind.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'ssh-keygen'],' ',[2,'-t ed25519'],' ',[3,'-C "you@example.com"']],[
 '<b>ssh-keygen.</b> Generates a new key pair in <code>~/.ssh/</code>.',
 '<b>-t (type).</b> Which kind of key. ed25519 is short, fast and secure.',
 '<b>-C (comment).</b> A label stuck on the public key so you know whose it is. Usually your email.'])}
${V.rules(V.rh('Rules'),
 V.ok('id_ed25519.pub','The .pub file is the one you paste into GitHub or a server'),V.no('sending id_ed25519','Never share, email or commit the private key'),
 V.ok('leaked? new pair','Delete it everywhere and generate a fresh pair'),
 V.rh('Conventions'),V.ok('a passphrase','Protects the private key if your laptop is stolen'))}
${V.hook(`Public is the padlock: give it away. Private is the key: never let it leave.`)}
`)}

${V.card(2,'Logging in with a key','what happens when you type ssh',`
${V.anat([[1,'ssh'],' ',[2,'deploy'],[3,'@'],[4,'203.0.113.20']],[
 '<b>ssh.</b> Secure Shell: an encrypted terminal on another machine.',
 '<b>User.</b> The account on the server, not on your laptop.',
 '<b>@</b> "at", like an email address.',
 '<b>Host.</b> The server\'s IP address or name.'])}
<p><b>Watch the handshake.</b> Your laptop is on the left, the server on the right.</p>
${V.steps([
 ['Once only: <b>ssh-copy-id</b> logs in with the password one last time and adds your public key to <b>~/.ssh/authorized_keys</b> on the server: its list of allowed padlocks.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 220" role="img" aria-label="ssh-copy-id copies the public key to the server"><rect class="bx-a" x="6" y="10" width="124" height="120" rx="8"/>${V.ic('laptop',28,16,80,'ic-a')}${V.ic('key',44,82,40,'ic-warn')}<text class="t-b" x="68" y="150" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">your laptop</text><rect class="bx" x="290" y="10" width="124" height="120" rx="8"/>${V.ic('server',312,16,80,'ic-info')}${V.ic('unlock',332,82,40,'ic-ok')}<text class="t-b" x="352" y="150" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">web1</text><path class="ln-a" d="M136 62H278"/><polygon class="ah-a" points="276,55 276,69 286,62"/><text class="t-m t-a" x="210" y="50" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700">copy .pub</text><text class="t" x="10" y="178" style="font-size:15px">$ ssh-copy-id deploy@203.0.113.20</text><rect class="bx-info" x="4" y="188" width="412" height="28" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="210" y="207" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">authorized_keys now holds your padlock</text></svg>`],
 ['Now <b>ssh deploy@203.0.113.20</b>. The server finds your padlock in its list and sends back a random challenge: "prove you hold the matching key".',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 220" role="img" aria-label="The server sends a random challenge"><rect class="bx-a" x="6" y="10" width="124" height="120" rx="8"/>${V.ic('laptop',28,16,80,'ic-a')}${V.ic('key',44,82,40,'ic-warn')}<text class="t-b" x="68" y="150" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">your laptop</text><rect class="bx" x="290" y="10" width="124" height="120" rx="8"/>${V.ic('server',312,16,80,'ic-info')}${V.ic('unlock',332,82,40,'ic-ok')}<text class="t-b" x="352" y="150" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">web1</text><path class="ln-a" d="M284 62H142"/><polygon class="ah-a" points="144,55 144,69 134,62"/><text class="t-m t-a" x="210" y="50" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700">challenge</text><text class="t" x="10" y="178" style="font-size:15px">$ ssh deploy@203.0.113.20</text><rect class="bx-info" x="4" y="188" width="412" height="28" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="210" y="207" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">server: prove you own the key</text></svg>`],
 ['Your laptop answers by <b>signing</b> the challenge with the private key. Only the signature travels. The private key never leaves your laptop.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 220" role="img" aria-label="The laptop sends back a signature made with the private key"><rect class="bx-a" x="6" y="10" width="124" height="120" rx="8"/>${V.ic('laptop',28,16,80,'ic-a')}${V.ic('key',44,82,40,'ic-warn')}<text class="t-b" x="68" y="150" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">your laptop</text><rect class="bx" x="290" y="10" width="124" height="120" rx="8"/>${V.ic('server',312,16,80,'ic-info')}${V.ic('unlock',332,82,40,'ic-ok')}<text class="t-b" x="352" y="150" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">web1</text><path class="ln-a" d="M136 62H278"/><polygon class="ah-a" points="276,55 276,69 286,62"/><text class="t-m t-a" x="210" y="50" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700">signature</text><text class="t" x="10" y="178" style="font-size:15px">signing with id_ed25519...</text><rect class="bx-info" x="4" y="188" width="412" height="28" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="210" y="207" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">the private key stays at home</text></svg>`],
 ['The server checks the signature with your public key. It matches, so you are in, with no password typed at all.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 220" role="img" aria-label="The signature matches and the server lets you in"><rect class="bx-a" x="6" y="10" width="124" height="120" rx="8"/>${V.ic('laptop',28,16,80,'ic-a')}${V.ic('key',44,82,40,'ic-warn')}<text class="t-b" x="68" y="150" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">your laptop</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="290" y="10" width="124" height="120" rx="8"/>${V.ic('server',312,16,80,'ic-ok')}${V.ic('unlock',332,82,40,'ic-ok')}<text class="t-b" x="352" y="150" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">web1</text><path class="ln-a" d="M284 62H142"/><polygon class="ah-a" points="144,55 144,69 134,62"/><text class="t-m t-a" x="210" y="50" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700">welcome</text><text class="t" x="10" y="178" style="font-size:15px">deploy@web1:~$</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="4" y="188" width="412" height="28" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="210" y="207" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">logged in with your key</text></svg>`]])}
${V.rules(V.ok('exit','Leave the server and come back to your own prompt'),V.ok('ssh -i ~/.ssh/work_key ...','-i picks a specific private key'),
 V.no('PasswordAuthentication yes','Once keys work, real servers switch passwords off in sshd_config'))}
${V.hook(`The server asks a question only your private key can answer, and the key never leaves home.`)}
`)}

${V.card(3,'scp and key permissions','copying files, and why SSH is fussy',`
${V.anat([[1,'scp'],' ',[2,'site.tar.gz'],' ',[3,'deploy@203.0.113.20'],[4,':'],[5,'~']],[
 '<b>scp.</b> "Secure copy": cp, but over SSH.',
 '<b>Source.</b> The file on your laptop.',
 '<b>Where.</b> The same user@host you use with ssh.',
 '<b>Colon.</b> Marks the remote side. Forget it and scp makes a local file called "deploy@203.0.113.20".',
 '<b>Remote path.</b> <code>~</code> is the deploy user\'s home folder.'])}
${V.why(`<p>If anyone else on your machine could read your private key, they could copy it and become you. So SSH refuses to use a key that has loose permissions, and makes you fix it.</p>`)}
${V.steps([
 ['You try a second key, <b>work_key</b>. SSH refuses to even use it, and tells you why.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 186" role="img" aria-label="ssh warns the key permissions are too open"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="174" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">$ ssh -i ~/.ssh/work_key deploy@203.0.113.20</text><text class="t-term t-bad" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">WARNING: UNPROTECTED PRIVATE KEY FILE!</text><text class="t-term t-bad" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">Permissions 0644 for '.../work_key'</text><text class="t-term t-bad" x="16" y="126" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">  are too open.</text><text class="t-term t-bad" x="16" y="156" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">This private key will be ignored.</text></svg>`],
 ['0644 means others can read it (the last 4 is r--). For a private key, that alone is a security hole. Lock it to you only.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 156" role="img" aria-label="chmod 600 fixes the key"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="144" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ chmod 600 ~/.ssh/work_key</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ ls -l ~/.ssh/work_key</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">-rw------- you you 98 work_key</text></svg>`],
 ['Try again: SSH accepts the key and logs you in.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 156" role="img" aria-label="login works with the fixed key"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="144" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">$ ssh -i ~/.ssh/work_key deploy@203.0.113.20</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">deploy@web1:~$</text></svg>`]])}
${V.rules(V.ok('chmod 600 private key','Only you can read or write it'),V.no('chmod 644 private key','Readable by everyone: SSH ignores it'),
 V.ok('chmod 700 ~/.ssh','The folder itself should be yours alone too'))}
${V.build(`<ol><li>Generate an ed25519 pair, pressing Enter at each question.</li><li>Install your public key on the server with ssh-copy-id (the last time you type the password).</li><li>Log in with plain ssh, notice there is no password prompt, then <code>exit</code>.</li><li>Copy the archive to the server's home folder with scp. Don't forget the colon.</li><li>Try the work key with <code>-i</code>, read the warning, fix it with chmod 600, and try again.</li></ol>`)}
${V.hook(`Private key: 600 or nothing.`)}
`)}

<div class="try"><b>Try it in your head</b>1. Which file goes into <code>authorized_keys</code>? <i>The public key, id_ed25519.pub.</i> 2. What is wrong with <code>scp site.tar.gz deploy@203.0.113.20</code>? <i>No colon, so it copies to a local file with that name.</i> 3. Does the private key travel to the server when you log in? <i>No, only a signature made with it.</i></div>
`);

